window.ETYME_MODEL={"parties":[{"meta":{"key":"client","number":"1","name":"Client","label":"Client","tagline":"The enterprise that buys, and never sells.","position":"Buys from everyone below — a prime, an integrator, a program office, a bench vendor, a consultant’s own corporation. Sells to nobody. The customer of the product, and the only party with no Customer lane: it is the customer.","desks":["Program Manager","Hiring Manager","Approver","HR Partner","Procurement Lead","AP Clerk","Compliance Officer","Viewer"],"doors":["Northbend","Athletic /demo · world-nike","Cavanaugh","Glassworks /demo · world-corning","Talvern","Medical /demo · world-terumo-bct"],"how":"","summary":"A client pays for the one thing none of its suppliers can give it: every contractor on its sites, across every supplier, with tenure added up, paperwork on file, hours signed and bills matched — from the desk of whoever does that job. In these drawings the client’s own desks are solid and every supplier collapses into one shaded lane: the client sees the rung it pays and nothing below it, unless its agreement demands disclosure. Shaded lane — a party outside the firm. Anything crossing into it is a document a counterparty reads. Blue-edged lane — one of this party’s own desks. Its boxes are solid; everyone else’s are faded but still there, because the stream does not change — only who is looking. Labelled arrow — the artifact that moves: requisition, submission, order, timesheet receipt, bill, invoice. Dashed box — a station the operating model names that the build does not yet do as a m"},"streams":[{"code":"L1.1","name":"Source to contract","lanes":[{"name":"Hiring Manager","sub":"raises · interviews · signs"},{"name":"HR Partner","sub":"reads the role · the plan"},{"name":"Procurement Lead","sub":"suppliers · band · release"},{"name":"Approver — the lead","sub":"cost center · signs the money"},{"name":"Program office","sub":"the rules · the plan"},{"name":"Your supplier","sub":"the firm you pay"},{"name":"Contractor","sub":"on your site, via a supplier"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Raise requisition","sub":"the role, the months, the rate","lane":"Hiring Manager"},{"n":2,"title":"HR reads the role","sub":"a contingent role? in the plan?","lane":"HR Partner"},{"n":3,"title":"Procurement audits","sub":"who may supply, at what band","lane":"Procurement Lead"},{"n":4,"title":"The lead signs the money","sub":"after both · else program office","lane":"Approver — the lead"},{"n":5,"title":"Within plan: by rule","sub":"every desk clears; no human","lane":"Program office"},{"n":6,"title":"Release to suppliers","sub":"the ones Procurement cleared","lane":"Procurement Lead"},{"n":7,"title":"Accept · pass down","sub":"a band of its own","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":8,"title":"Source & match","sub":"a score says why","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":9,"title":"Consent to represent","sub":"the listing — yours to give","lane":"Contractor"},{"n":10,"title":"Submit","sub":"a rate, at this rung","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":11,"title":"Shortlist · negotiate","sub":"right-to-work first","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":12,"title":"Interview","sub":"rounds in turn","lane":"Hiring Manager"},{"n":13,"title":"Award","sub":"the order and its first line","lane":"Hiring Manager"}],"refusals":[{"text":"a supplier cannot award its own","lane":"Hiring Manager","station":13},{"text":"names nobody’s suppliers","lane":"HR Partner","station":2},{"text":"a hiring manager cannot choose who sees it","lane":"Procurement Lead","station":6},{"text":"nobody signs their own — the raiser least of all","lane":"Approver — the lead","station":4}],"caption":"One requisition becomes one award. It clears three desks first — HR reads the role, Procurement audits the suppliers, the lead who owns the cost center signs the money — and nobody signs their own; within plan every desk clears by rule and it publishes itself. Every arrow that crosses into a shaded lane is a document a counterparty reads — and the rate band travels on the invitation, never on the requisition, so no supplier reads another’s.","short":"Source to contract","page":7,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Requisition","sap":"a purchase requisition · a job posting","note":"Same object. Etyme clears it through three desks — HR reads the role, Procurement audits the suppliers, the cost-center lead signs the money; SAP puts a release strategy on it."},{"etyme":"Rate band","sap":"a rate guideline · a price on the vendor record","note":"Both keep the price per supplier where no other supplier can read it. Etyme puts it on the invitation."},{"etyme":"Supplier release","sap":"a request for quotation to the source list","note":"“These vendors may quote.” The program office decides, never the hiring manager."},{"etyme":"Bench listing — consent to be marketed","sap":"—","note":"No SAP word. Fieldglass has a worker profile; nobody in SAP consents to be sold. The invariant with no counterpart."},{"etyme":"Submission","sap":"a quotation · a job-seeker submittal","note":"A quotation at a rate, one per rung of the chain — two rows, one chain."},{"etyme":"Interview","sap":"an interview","note":"Only whoever is hiring may set up or decide a round."},{"etyme":"Award","sap":"creating the purchase order · creating the work order","note":"In SAP the award *is* the order. Etyme’s award now raises the order and writes the contract as its first line."},{"etyme":"Requirement going down a chain","sap":"a tiered supplier · subcontracting","note":"The prime retypes the role for its sub under a band of its own; the sub never learns the end client unless the agreement requires disclosure."},{"etyme":"Within plan: by rule — every desk clears; no human · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/ask-for-person.test.ts asking for a person you were shown › a candidate who was submitted and not hired is on the register with everything the client knows, and the read leaves a trail somebody never put in front of this client cannot be opened, and the refusal is logged too asking for him on a published role goes to the supplier on the thread for that role, and says so a role that is not published cannot be asked for, and neither can a role he is already on · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/client-programme.test.ts 1 · the hiring manager posts a requirement › a role inside plan and under every line opens itself — nobody has to approve it · run: Chapter 1 — a one-person corporation registers on a gmail address › own consultant, listed on their own bench · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/full-spine.test.ts Step 1 — a manager at Auralis raises a requisition › is routed to an approver rather than opened, because it is worth $288,000 a year is not open to a single vendor until somebody has said yes records why it routed, in words the manager can read","sap":"asking for somebody you buy through a chain › belongs to the firm below the one Nike pays asking for her opens the thread with the prime Nike pays, and never with the sub-vendor holding reading a name is not having a channel her and nothing in the reply, the thread title, the message or its metadata names the firm below the suppliers and not the firm holding them rung Nike pays a role over the plan and over the line waits on HR's read of the role, then the money — and the manager who raised it cannot wave it through the release can only go to the suppliers Procurement cleared ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/first-real-transaction.test.ts the owner is already their a company of one has one role, and it is Owner Step 3 — Auralis puts it in front of its MSP, with a band › does not echo the band back in the response, where a second vendor could read it refuses a band above the ceiling the requisition itself was approved at","note":"the bench listing that would be submitted against the prime is told who was asked for and on which role, and why it came to them a client whose agreement discloses sub-vendor names still asks through the prime, because somebody Nike has never bought through anyone is refused in a sentence that names Nike’s own a blocked person cannot be asked for until the block is lifted 2 · the program office sends it to suppliers, and a supplier answers › the program office sends it to Pinnacle with a band Pinnacle alone can see Pinnacle puts Tariq forward sends it to Maren and nobody else Step 4 — Maren takes it on and passes it down the panel › writes its own record of the role, carrying Auralis forward as the end client Step 5 — Computer Systems takes it on and asks its sub-vendor › sends it to CloudEPA at a third band, $20 below what Auralis will pay"}],"png":"img/model/client-p7.png","sentences":73},{"code":"L1.2","name":"Contract to onboard","lanes":[{"name":"Hiring Manager","sub":"raises · interviews · signs"},{"name":"Procurement Lead","sub":"suppliers · band · release"},{"name":"Program office","sub":"the rules · the plan"},{"name":"Your supplier","sub":"the firm you pay"},{"name":"Contractor","sub":"on your site, via a supplier"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Agreement, if new","sub":"both sign · optional","lane":"Program office"},{"n":2,"title":"Countersign","sub":"the later date counts","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":3,"title":"Purchase order","sub":"the header · a ceiling","lane":"Procurement Lead"},{"n":4,"title":"Sell line","sub":"this person, this rate","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":5,"title":"Buy line","sub":"pays the sub, or payroll","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":6,"title":"Own W2 — no order","sub":"employment is the paper","lane":"Contractor"},{"n":7,"title":"Candidate green","sub":"I-9 · check · license","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":8,"title":"Papers","sub":"a link · no sign-in","lane":"Contractor"},{"n":9,"title":"Company green","sub":"insurance · terms","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":10,"title":"Activate","sub":"both lines move","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":11,"title":"Start date announced","sub":"not yet a moment","lane":"Hiring Manager"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"Two gates, not one: the candidate is green and the company is green. The buy line forks — an order to a sub-vendor carries a ceiling; an employment to your own W2 carries no order at all, because you do not raise a purchase order to your own employee.","short":"Contract to onboard","page":10,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Agreement · MSA","sap":"an outline agreement · a sales contract","note":"Optional since 2026-09-18. Both signatures, and the date that matters is the later one. SAP has no countersignature of its own; that lives in a contracts tool. Never “master agreement” on a screen — “master contract” is the profitability roll-up, a different thing."},{"etyme":"Purchase order · sales order · work order","sap":"one order, mirrored: a PO on the buyer, a sales order on the seller","note":"One row, three names. The header: counterparty, ceiling, dates, terms, the four partner roles."},{"etyme":"Sell line — bills the customer","sap":"a sales-order item, one per worker","note":"A line on the order: this person, this rate, this site. What the firm bills from."},{"etyme":"Buy line to a sub-vendor — pays by invoice receipt","sap":"a service item on our order to the vendor","note":"Draws down our order to the sub. Rhythm and terms read from the document; the dates are the line’s own, because a line is a person."},{"etyme":"Buy line to own W2 — pays by payroll","sap":"a hiring action, not a vendor record","note":"No order to your own employee. SAP files the person under HR, never under purchasing."},{"etyme":"Supplier onboarding — four desks","sap":"supplier registration and qualification","note":"Etyme walks department lead, Procurement, HR and Finance in order, each verifying only its own items."},{"etyme":"Work authorization · I-9","sap":"a residence-status record on the person","note":"BLOCK. The form has an edition; an I-9 with nothing behind it is not held."},{"etyme":"Certificate of insurance","sap":"a supplier certificate with a validity window","note":"Etyme reads the start date as a floor — cover beginning next month does not cover somebody starting this week."},{"etyme":"Compliance · Agreement · Proof","sap":"—","note":"Etyme’s three purposes decide behavior. SAP scatters them across HR, procurement and document management."},{"etyme":"Activate","sap":"the hire · the release","note":"Both lines move together. Payment terms are not yet a gate."},{"etyme":"Start date announced — not yet a moment · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/agreement-lifecycle.test.ts a master agreement gets a term, a signature and a trail › a recruiter cannot change the payment days or the margin floor, and is told who can a client reading the supplier’s agreement is told whose terms they are, and cannot change them changing the payment days records what they were before, who changed them and why an amendment writes an automation log naming what moved and why re-saving the same payment days is refused rather than written to the trail as an amendment a signature can no longer be typed in as a bare date — the refusal says to record who signed recording the term says in a sentence when the agreement runs out and how many days that is recording the executed document keeps the file and its name on the agreement, not in somebody’s email a link that is not a link is refused, and the refusal says what a link looks like · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/award-order.test.ts A client awards, and the order it will quote exists the same second › the purchase order the client will read, with the contract as its first line the client reads it as a purchase order and the supplier reads the same row as its sales order","sap":"one signature does not execute an agreement — it says which side still owes a counter-signature an agreement that renews itself rolls its end date on instead of lapsing, and the trail says it did the same side cannot sign twice, and the refusal says to amend rather than sign again a signature with no title is refused, because whether the signer had authority is the first thing a recruiter cannot end an agreement either anybody asks the counter-signature executes the agreement, dated the later of the two, and says nothing here on verified it the history answers what the payment days were before they were changed, and what they are now asking what the terms were before the agreement existed returns nothing rather than today’s terms a client reading the history sees the payment days and never the supplier’s margin floor the nightly job marks an agreement running out and tells the contracting desk at thirty days running the nightly job again does not say the same thing twice awarding a submission raises the order’s ceiling is what the requisition was approved at, never a third number says where the ceiling came from, in a sentence anybody can audit a line never disagrees with its header on the day it is written","note":"ending an agreement without saying why is refused ending an agreement with people still working under it says how many, and lets their contracts run the terms of an agreement that was ended can no longer be changed an agreement that was ended cannot be ended twice, and the calendar never revives it the agreements screen shows an ended agreement as ended, with people still working under it as the worst thing on the row reading the agreements screen leaves an access log for the people it names an award with no agreement in place records one marked as never papered, rather than refusing the placement runs a month past the last day of the work, so the final invoice has an order to quote carries where the work happens and who recorded it never decides for the client that silence approves a timesheet"}],"png":"img/model/client-p10.png","sentences":152},{"code":"L1.3","name":"Work to approve","lanes":[{"name":"Hiring Manager","sub":"raises · interviews · signs"},{"name":"Program office","sub":"the rules · the plan"},{"name":"Your supplier","sub":"the firm you pay"},{"name":"Contractor","sub":"on your site, via a supplier"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"File the week","sub":"your own hours","lane":"Contractor"},{"n":2,"title":"Expense","sub":"receipt attached","lane":"Contractor"},{"n":3,"title":"Timesheet receipt","sub":"the goods receipt, here","lane":"Hiring Manager"},{"n":4,"title":"Silence counts?","sub":"if the order says so","lane":"Program office"},{"n":5,"title":"Checked vs contract","sub":"over hours · past end","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":6,"title":"Employer acceptance","sub":"what we will pay for","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":7,"title":"Milestone accepted","sub":"a receipt of another shape","lane":"Hiring Manager"}],"refusals":[{"text":"nobody signs their own hours","lane":"Hiring Manager","station":3}],"caption":"The goods receipt of a staffing firm is the signed week. SAP calls it a service entry sheet; the founder named it a timesheet receipt, and the screens use his word. Two signatures from two companies, one row of hours, never one per hop.","short":"Work to approve","page":14,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Timesheet","sap":"a time sheet","note":"The worker files their own week; the agency may enter on their behalf, nobody may sign for them."},{"etyme":"Timesheet receipt — client approval","sap":"the service entry sheet — the goods receipt for services","note":"Same object. “Our goods receipt equivalent is timesheet receipt or expense receipt.” The trade’s word wins on the screen."},{"etyme":"Employer acceptance","sap":"releasing the time sheet for pay","note":"SAP has one approval. Etyme has two signatures, because the client says the work happened and the employer says what it will pay for — different statements."},{"etyme":"Pass-through","sap":"tiered approval","note":"Each rung between the client and the worker sees the same hours it will bill and be billed for."},{"etyme":"Expense receipt","sap":"an expense report","note":"An approved, client-billable expense rides the next bill as a line of its own."},{"etyme":"Milestone receipt","sap":"a milestone on a billing plan","note":"Acceptance is the receipt; it bills as a milestone line."},{"etyme":"Auto-approval","sap":"an approval rule","note":"Read off the order: “silence counts” with a window. It fired for the first time on 2026-09-17, because no order row had ever existed to carry the flag."},{"etyme":"A week checked against its contract","sap":"—","note":"Over the role’s hours or past the last day says so in a sentence before anybody signs; “Approve anyway” takes a reason."}],"png":"img/model/client-p14.png","sentences":30},{"code":"L1.4","name":"Approve to invoice","lanes":[{"name":"AP Clerk","sub":"matches and pays bills"},{"name":"Your supplier","sub":"the firm you pay"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Raise the bill","sub":"from the sell line","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":2,"title":"Four partners","sub":"sold-to · bill-to · ship-to · payer","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":3,"title":"Receives","sub":"receipt starts the clock","lane":"AP Clerk"},{"n":4,"title":"Pays what matched","sub":"never an unmatched bill","lane":"AP Clerk"},{"n":5,"title":"Cash application","sub":"a short payment is a question","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":6,"title":"Age & dun","sub":"from the due date, not period end","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":7,"title":"Dispute → credit note","sub":"reverses revenue","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":8,"title":"Exposure & limit","sub":"unpaid + unbilled + committed","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":9,"title":"Collections","sub":"stop-work · write-off","lane":"Your supplier"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"The firm bills its customer — SAP’s process is literally called billing, and the founder’s word matches it. The due date belongs to the document, counted from the day the client received it; nothing schedules one on the calendar to disagree with it.","short":"Approve to invoice","page":16,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Bill","sap":"billing — a billing document, a customer invoice","note":"Aligned by decision: “companies bill (also called invoice) a customer.”"},{"etyme":"Bill line — hours · expense · milestone","sap":"a billing item","note":"Three receipts, three kinds of line, one match."},{"etyme":"Sold-to · bill-to · ship-to · payer","sap":"the four partner roles on a sales document","note":"Identical concept. The first thing a large enterprise asks for."},{"etyme":"Tax","sap":"a tax code with a place of supply","note":"Regime, outcome and place of supply as queryable fields — a return cannot be filed from a blob."},{"etyme":"Cash application","sap":"an incoming payment · a lockbox","note":"A part payment is chased for the balance; a short payment is a question for a person, not arrears."},{"etyme":"Aging","sap":"customer open items","note":"Aged from the day each bill fell due, so sixty-day terms are not late on day forty-five."},{"etyme":"Dunning","sap":"a dunning run","note":"The ladder; who owns each step is a desk."},{"etyme":"Credit note","sap":"a credit memo","note":"A customer document we issue; it reverses revenue. Posted into the bill’s own period."},{"etyme":"Exposure · limit · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/client-programme.test.ts 3 · the hiring manager awards, and both contracts exist with their due dates › award its own candidate the award writes the sell contract, the buy contract, the link and the cycles · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/desks-in-tandem.test.ts","sap":"credit management a supplier cannot 6 · Pinnacle invoices; Northbend Athletic pays what matched › signed week — 40 hours at $38 Brightmoor cannot raise an invoice on Pinnacle's engagement the clerk cannot pay an invoice the supplier has not submitted through the match","note":"Exposure is unpaid plus delivered-not-billed plus committed for the rest of every running assignment — which is why a client owing a little can be the riskiest name on the list. Pinnacle raises the invoice from the Pinnacle submits it; the invoice matches the hours a firm that is not on the invoice cannot pay it, and is not told it exists the compliance officer cannot pay it either — reading is not paying"}],"png":"img/model/client-p16.png","sentences":23},{"code":"L1.5","name":"Approve to pay","lanes":[{"name":"Your supplier","sub":"the firm you pay"},{"name":"Contractor","sub":"on your site, via a supplier"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Issues its invoice","sub":"their number, not ours","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":2,"title":"Invoice receipt","sub":"received, never raised","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":3,"title":"Three-way match","sub":"order ↔ receipt ↔ invoice","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":4,"title":"Exception → desk","sub":"a decision, with a reason","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":5,"title":"Payment run","sub":"approver is not the raiser","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":6,"title":"Remittance","sub":"what was paid, for what","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":7,"title":"Payroll","sub":"on accepted hours only","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":8,"title":"Paid","sub":"own pay · never the bill rate","lane":"Contractor"},{"n":9,"title":"Tax data → bureau","sub":"1099 · W-2 data","lane":"Your supplier"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"Money out in two directions, two words. A supplier’s invoice is received and matched — the invoice-receipt step. An employee is paid by payroll, which Fieldglass never touches because it stops at the supplier. The candidate sees what they are paid and never what a firm above them charges.","short":"Approve to pay","page":18,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Invoice receipt","sap":"invoice verification — the supplier’s invoice, received and matched","note":"The founder’s term is SAP’s term. The supplier issues the document; we receive it. Receiving it cannot need the permission to issue one of ours."},{"etyme":"Three-way match","sap":"order ↔ goods receipt ↔ invoice receipt","note":"Identical. Work order ↔ timesheet receipt ↔ supplier invoice. A client pays what came through the match."},{"etyme":"Match exception → the AP desk","sap":"a blocked invoice, released by a person","note":"A bill that did not match is a decision, with a reason recorded."},{"etyme":"Payment run","sap":"the automatic payment run","note":"An approver who is not the raiser."},{"etyme":"Remittance","sap":"a payment advice","note":""},{"etyme":"Payroll","sap":"payroll","note":"Fieldglass does not pay workers; it stops at the supplier. Payroll is the supplier’s own system."},{"etyme":"Pay model","sap":"wage types","note":"Salary, hourly, C2C, commission — applied per line."},{"etyme":"Bench reserve","sap":"—","note":"No SAP word. A firm holding back against bench time between projects."},{"etyme":"1099 · W-2 data","sap":"withholding and year-end reporting","note":"Data for the bureau, not the filing."},{"etyme":"Pay day shifts back; bill day shifts forward · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/client-programme.test.ts 4 · nobody starts without paperwork › the AP clerk is a party and still cannot start somebody — that is not the clerk's job","sap":"a factory calendar · payment terms 5 · Tariq files a week; the hiring manager signs it ›","note":"Per company, per category — before, after or neither — decided 2026-09-17 and wired into the dates the same day. the AP clerk cannot enter hours for him 6 · Pinnacle invoices; Northbend Athletic pays what matched › the AP clerk pays it, and the payment says who paid whom"}],"png":"img/model/client-p18.png","sentences":10},{"code":"L1.6","name":"Record to report","lanes":[{"name":"Your supplier","sub":"the firm you pay"},{"name":"Your books","sub":"where the program’s costs land"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Receipt posted","sub":"cost · payable","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":2,"title":"Payroll posted","sub":"pay · burden","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":3,"title":"Journal","sub":"one balanced entry each","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":4,"title":"Master contract","sub":"optional tag · the roll-up","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":5,"title":"Profitability","sub":"margin, by the deal","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":6,"title":"Earned vs cash","sub":"days to get paid, real months","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":7,"title":"Account map","sub":"our words → their accounts","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":8,"title":"Outbound posting","sub":"to the books they keep","lane":"Your books"},{"n":9,"title":"Reconciliation","sub":"read back, differences owned","lane":"Your books"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"Etyme posts into the books; it does not replace them. The mapping is stated once at the boundary: QuickBooks and Xero say Invoice for the customer document and Bill for the received one — their Invoice is our bill, their Bill is our invoice receipt.","short":"Record to report","page":20,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Journal","sap":"the general ledger · a universal journal","note":"Every posting turns into a balanced entry; the receivable move on every bill and the cash move on every applied receipt."},{"etyme":"The pair — a sell line and the buy line that funds it","sap":"a sales item and a purchase item settled to one cost object","note":"A placement’s own margin. Always written by the award, because a buy line pays for some sell line."},{"etyme":"Master contract — the profitability roll-up","sap":"an internal order · a work-breakdown element","note":"The Etyme-2017 word, kept: the container that once held both sides on one row is now an optional tag. A company tags sell and buy lines to one when it wants to see the deal’s margin. Not a commercial document; nobody signs one — same in SAP, where the sales order and the purchase order both settle to it."},{"etyme":"Profitability by pair, person, customer, master","sap":"margin analysis","note":"Read from real revenue and cost; gated on the right to read P&L, which the account manager deliberately does not hold."},{"etyme":"Earned against cash","sap":"revenue recognition","note":"Days to get paid counted back through real months rather than divided by an average, so growth does not move it."},{"etyme":"Currency","sap":"currency types and exchange rates","note":"Money in minor units, always."},{"etyme":"ERP account map","sap":"the chart of accounts · an integration","note":"Businesses pay for QuickBooks, SAP and NetSuite directly; Etyme posts to them."},{"etyme":"Reconciliation · run: Chapter 4 — a week is worked and approved by both parties › the approval posted real money to a real project order · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/full-spine.test.ts","sap":"clearing · a bank statement ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/first-real-transaction.test.ts Chapter 6 — the money is visible where a person would look for it › margin, not a fabricated one","note":"Reads the books back; a difference is a row somebody owns. profitability reports the real"}],"png":"img/model/client-p20.png","sentences":20},{"code":"L1.7","name":"Govern and protect","lanes":[{"name":"Compliance Officer","sub":"tenure · authorization"},{"name":"Your supplier","sub":"the firm you pay"},{"name":"Etyme, unprompted","sub":"what it does on its own"},{"name":"Contractor","sub":"on your site, via a supplier"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Tenure ledger","sub":"the person, at the client","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":2,"title":"Days on site","sub":"counted once per day","lane":"Compliance Officer"},{"n":3,"title":"Classification","sub":"W2 · 1099 · C2C","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":4,"title":"Approval chains","sub":"by rule and by name","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":5,"title":"Segregation","sub":"nobody decides two desks","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":6,"title":"Supplier standing","sub":"probation · approved · preferred","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":7,"title":"Concentration","sub":"one client, one person","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":8,"title":"Access log","sub":"every read · refusals too","lane":"Etyme, unprompted"},{"n":9,"title":"Automation log","sub":"why · and can it be undone","lane":"Etyme, unprompted"},{"n":10,"title":"Do-not-return list","sub":"the company’s own","lane":"Your supplier"},{"n":11,"title":"Told what is held","sub":"own pay only","lane":"Contractor"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"The moat, not the wedge: tenure accrues to the person at the client across every supplier, counted once per day on site. SAP records what changed; Etyme also records why, and whether it can be undone — and every read of another person’s data leaves a row, including the refusals.","short":"Govern and protect","page":22,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Tenure — the person at the client, across suppliers","sap":"a tenure policy · contract elements on the person","note":"Fieldglass tracks tenure per worker at the buyer within its own walls. Etyme’s claim is across suppliers who are not all on one system — which is every buyer who cannot afford one."},{"etyme":"Worker classification","sap":"employee group and subgroup","note":"BLOCK where legally grounded."},{"etyme":"Approval chain","sap":"a release strategy · a workflow","note":"Most requisitions must clear without a human. A desk nobody named falls back; it never refuses."},{"etyme":"Segregation of duties","sap":"an access-control ruleset","note":"“You recommended this firm, so the desks decide it without you.” A sentence, never a disabled button."},{"etyme":"Supplier standing","sap":"supplier risk","note":"Probation · approved · preferred, read by the tier rule."},{"etyme":"Concentration","sap":"margin analysis by customer","note":"Revenue share riding on one client, one supplier, one person, with a named risk owner."},{"etyme":"Access log — every read of a person","sap":"an audit log · read-access logging","note":"The nearest thing logs reads of sensitive fields. Etyme logs the refusals too."},{"etyme":"Company walls","sap":"authorization objects · company codes","note":"A caller with no company is refused, never handed every company’s list."},{"etyme":"Automation log — what the system did on its own","sap":"change documents","note":"SAP records what changed. Etyme records the plain-English reason and an honest reversible flag, and every action name is declared on a ladder."},{"etyme":"Do-not-return list","sap":"a vendor block · a rehire flag","note":"Read by every desk that puts people forward; written by the desk that owns who goes forward. Never read across companies."},{"etyme":"Whose rate is on the row","sap":"rate visibility","note":"The person named on a sell line is the subject of it, not a party to it."},{"etyme":"What we tell people about their data","sap":"information lifecycle · data privacy","note":"A page of their own, off until they turn it on."},{"etyme":"Days on site — counted once per day · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/client-programme.test.ts 7 · tenure is the person's, across every supplier › Lucía has fourteen months at Northbend Athletic — thirteen through Brightmoor, one through Pinnacle — and Pinnacle knows only the one Kwame is over the cap and inside the break — the ledger shows the date he is eligible · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/desks-in-tandem.test.ts the desks, in tandem: one placement, and at every station the wrong desk is refused › reads what the placement made, and the recruiter — who cannot see what anyone costs — cannot · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/full-spine.test.ts Step 5 — Computer Systems takes it on and asks its sub-vendor › leaves CloudEPA unable to see what Auralis agreed to pay · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/party-uniform.test.ts the grid itself › every one of the eight positions has a firm and somebody who can sign in as it","sap":"at Talvern Medical, Anders is twenty-three months on site across two suppliers against a cap of asking somebody back is a date inside the break, and a button after it eighteen a person supplied through a prime and a bench vendor is counted once, not once per rung the owner Step 20 — what each firm made › leaves Auralis unable to see CloudEPA anywhere in its own program a position is what a firm is on this deal, never a column on the firm","note":"the compliance officer sees which supplier's cover is about to run out every one of those reads left a trail Step 21 — one placement, opened, top to bottom › writes an access log row for the refusal as well as the read"}],"png":"img/model/client-p22.png","sentences":108}]},{"meta":{"key":"prime","number":"4","name":"Prime vendor","label":"Prime vendor","tagline":"Sells to the client. Buys from a sub-vendor by order, or its own W2 with none.","position":"Sells to the client on a purchase order the client raises and it reads as its sales order. Buys from a sub-vendor on an order of its own, or brings its own W2 with no order. Both sides of a placement are its to administer, and the sub- vendor’s name is its to keep.","desks":["Owner","Admin","Recruiter","Resource Manager","Account Manager","HR","Contract Manager","Accounts Receivable","AP & Payroll","Finance","Compliance Officer"],"doors":["Computer","Systems","Inc /demo · world-computer-systems","Vertex","Global /demo · world-vertex-global"],"how":"","summary":"The base drawing. A prime is the party that trades with all three counterparties — a customer above, supply below, and the person the work is about — which is why every other party in this set is described as this drawing with lanes removed or a leg missing. The founder’s operating model was stated from this desk: recruiters procure and submit, account managers sell upward, contract manager and HR make both sides compliant, the client signs the week, the firm bills its customer, pays its people and its suppliers, and ownership reads the margin. Shaded lane — a party outside the firm. Anything crossing into it is a document a counterparty reads. Blue-edged lane — one of this party’s own desks. Its boxes are solid; everyone else’s are faded but still there, because the stream does not change — only who is looking. Labelled arrow — the artifact that moves: requisition, submission, order, ti"},"streams":[{"code":"L1.1","name":"Source to contract","lanes":[{"name":"The client","sub":"the end customer you bill"},{"name":"Account Manager","sub":"sells upward"},{"name":"Recruiter","sub":"procures profiles"},{"name":"Your sub-vendor","sub":"its name is yours to keep"},{"name":"Candidate","sub":"a sub’s person, or your own W2"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Raise requisition","sub":"the role, the months, the rate","lane":"The client"},{"n":2,"title":"Three desks clear it","sub":"HR · Procurement · the lead","lane":"The client"},{"n":3,"title":"Release to suppliers","sub":"the ones Procurement cleared","lane":"The client"},{"n":4,"title":"Accept · pass down","sub":"a band of its own","lane":"Account Manager"},{"n":5,"title":"Sub records the role","sub":"its own record of it","lane":"Your sub-vendor"},{"n":6,"title":"Source & match","sub":"a score says why","lane":"Recruiter"},{"n":7,"title":"Consent to represent","sub":"the listing — yours to give","lane":"Candidate"},{"n":8,"title":"Submit","sub":"a rate, at this rung","lane":"Recruiter"},{"n":9,"title":"Shortlist · negotiate","sub":"right-to-work first","lane":"Account Manager"},{"n":10,"title":"Interview","sub":"rounds in turn","lane":"The client"},{"n":11,"title":"Award","sub":"the order and its first line","lane":"The client"}],"refusals":[{"text":"no listing, no submission — unless own W2","lane":"Recruiter","station":8}],"caption":"One requisition becomes one award. It clears three desks first — HR reads the role, Procurement audits the suppliers, the lead who owns the cost center signs the money — and nobody signs their own; within plan every desk clears by rule and it publishes itself. Every arrow that crosses into a shaded lane is a document a counterparty reads — and the rate band travels on the invitation, never on the requisition, so no supplier reads another’s.","short":"Source to contract","page":2,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Requisition","sap":"a purchase requisition · a job posting","note":"Same object. Etyme clears it through three desks — HR reads the role, Procurement audits the suppliers, the cost-center lead signs the money; SAP puts a release strategy on it."},{"etyme":"Rate band","sap":"a rate guideline · a price on the vendor record","note":"Both keep the price per supplier where no other supplier can read it. Etyme puts it on the invitation."},{"etyme":"Supplier release","sap":"a request for quotation to the source list","note":"“These vendors may quote.” The program office decides, never the hiring manager."},{"etyme":"Bench listing — consent to be marketed","sap":"—","note":"No SAP word. Fieldglass has a worker profile; nobody in SAP consents to be sold. The invariant with no counterpart."},{"etyme":"Submission","sap":"a quotation · a job-seeker submittal","note":"A quotation at a rate, one per rung of the chain — two rows, one chain."},{"etyme":"Interview","sap":"an interview","note":"Only whoever is hiring may set up or decide a round."},{"etyme":"Award","sap":"creating the purchase order · creating the work order","note":"In SAP the award *is* the order. Etyme’s award now raises the order and writes the contract as its first line."},{"etyme":"Requirement going down a chain","sap":"a tiered supplier · subcontracting","note":"The prime retypes the role for its sub under a band of its own; the sub never learns the end client unless the agreement requires disclosure."}],"png":"img/model/prime-p2.png","sentences":73},{"code":"L1.2","name":"Contract to onboard","lanes":[{"name":"The client","sub":"the end customer you bill"},{"name":"Account Manager","sub":"sells upward"},{"name":"Contract Manager","sub":"papers it"},{"name":"HR","sub":"candidate & supplier standing"},{"name":"Your sub-vendor","sub":"its name is yours to keep"},{"name":"Candidate","sub":"a sub’s person, or your own W2"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Agreement, if new","sub":"both sign · optional","lane":"The client"},{"n":2,"title":"Countersign","sub":"the later date counts","lane":"Account Manager"},{"n":3,"title":"Purchase order","sub":"the header · a ceiling","lane":"The client"},{"n":4,"title":"Sell line","sub":"this person, this rate","lane":"Contract Manager"},{"n":5,"title":"Buy line","sub":"pays the sub, or payroll","lane":"Contract Manager"},{"n":6,"title":"Our order to the sub","sub":"a ceiling of its own","lane":"Your sub-vendor"},{"n":7,"title":"Own W2 — no order","sub":"employment is the paper","lane":"Candidate"},{"n":8,"title":"Candidate green","sub":"I-9 · check · license","lane":"HR"},{"n":9,"title":"Papers","sub":"a link · no sign-in","lane":"Candidate"},{"n":10,"title":"Company green","sub":"insurance · terms","lane":"HR"},{"n":11,"title":"Insurance certificate","sub":"the start date is a floor","lane":"Your sub-vendor"},{"n":12,"title":"Activate","sub":"both lines move","lane":"Contract Manager"},{"n":13,"title":"Start date announced","sub":"not yet a moment","lane":"The client"}],"refusals":[{"text":"no I-9, no start · lapsed cover blocks","lane":"Contract Manager","station":12}],"caption":"Two gates, not one: the candidate is green and the company is green. The buy line forks — an order to a sub-vendor carries a ceiling; an employment to your own W2 carries no order at all, because you do not raise a purchase order to your own employee.","short":"Contract to onboard","page":4,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Agreement · MSA","sap":"an outline agreement · a sales contract","note":"Optional since 2026-09-18. Both signatures, and the date that matters is the later one. SAP has no countersignature of its own; that lives in a contracts tool. Never “master agreement” on a screen — “master contract” is the profitability roll-up, a different thing."},{"etyme":"Purchase order · sales order · work order","sap":"one order, mirrored: a PO on the buyer, a sales order on the seller","note":"One row, three names. The header: counterparty, ceiling, dates, terms, the four partner roles."},{"etyme":"Sell line — bills the customer","sap":"a sales-order item, one per worker","note":"A line on the order: this person, this rate, this site. What the firm bills from."},{"etyme":"Buy line to a sub-vendor — pays by invoice receipt","sap":"a service item on our order to the vendor","note":"Draws down our order to the sub. Rhythm and terms read from the document; the dates are the line’s own, because a line is a person."},{"etyme":"Buy line to own W2 — pays by payroll","sap":"a hiring action, not a vendor record","note":"No order to your own employee. SAP files the person under HR, never under purchasing."},{"etyme":"Supplier onboarding — four desks","sap":"supplier registration and qualification","note":"Etyme walks department lead, Procurement, HR and Finance in order, each verifying only its own items."},{"etyme":"Work authorization · I-9","sap":"a residence-status record on the person","note":"BLOCK. The form has an edition; an I-9 with nothing behind it is not held."},{"etyme":"Certificate of insurance","sap":"a supplier certificate with a validity window","note":"Etyme reads the start date as a floor — cover beginning next month does not cover somebody starting this week."},{"etyme":"Compliance · Agreement · Proof","sap":"—","note":"Etyme’s three purposes decide behavior. SAP scatters them across HR, procurement and document management."},{"etyme":"Activate · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/agreement-lifecycle.test.ts a master agreement gets a term, a signature and a trail › a recruiter cannot change the payment days or the margin floor, and is told who can a client reading the supplier’s agreement is told whose terms they are, and cannot change them changing the payment days records what they were before, who changed them and why an amendment writes an automation log naming what moved and why re-saving the same payment days is refused rather than written to the trail as an amendment a signature can no longer be typed in as a bare date — the refusal says to record who signed recording the term says in a sentence when the agreement runs out and how many days that is recording the executed document keeps the file and its name on the agreement, not in somebody’s email a link that is not a link is refused, and the refusal says what a link looks like · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/award-order.test.ts A client awards, and the order it will quote exists the same second › the purchase order the client will read, with the contract as its first line the client reads it as a purchase order and the supplier reads the same row as its sales order the order’s ceiling is what the requisition was approved at, never a third number says where the ceiling came from, in a sentence anybody can audit a line never disagrees with its header on the day it is written runs a month past the last day of the work, so the final invoice has an order to quote","sap":"the hire · the release one signature does not execute an agreement — it says which side still owes a counter-signature an agreement that renews itself rolls its end date on instead of lapsing, and the trail says it did the same side cannot sign twice, and the refusal says to amend rather than sign again a signature with no title is refused, because whether the signer had authority is the first thing a recruiter cannot end an agreement either anybody asks the counter-signature executes the agreement, dated the later of the two, and says nothing here on verified it the history answers what the payment days were before they were changed, and what they are now asking what the terms were before the agreement existed returns nothing rather than today’s terms a client reading the history sees the payment days and never the supplier’s margin floor the nightly job marks an agreement running out and tells the contracting desk at thirty days running the nightly job again does not say the same thing twice awarding a submission raises carries where the work happens and who recorded it never decides for the client that silence approves a timesheet an award with no agreement behind it writes no agreement, and the placement stands on the order the ceiling is not quietly raised to fit the second person — that is the client’s own act alone an employee’s line hangs on no order at all Five people on one commitment is one document with five lines › same client goes on the same order as a second line","note":"Both lines move together. Payment terms are not yet a gate. ending an agreement without saying why is refused ending an agreement with people still working under it says how many, and lets their contracts run the terms of an agreement that was ended can no longer be changed an agreement that was ended cannot be ended twice, and the calendar never revives it the agreements screen shows an ended agreement as ended, with people still working under it as the worst thing on the row reading the agreements screen leaves an access log for the people it names an award with no agreement in place records one marked as never papered, rather than refusing the placement the second award joins the engagement the first one opened, so one deal is not billed as two does not raise a second order to the same supplier, so the client has one number to quote an engagement of the same name between two other firms is never joined, because the lines underneath say whose it is a second person awarded to the A prime buys below the line it sells › gives the sub-vendor’s placement its own order, from the prime to the sub"}],"png":"img/model/prime-p4.png","sentences":183},{"code":"L1.3","name":"Work to approve","lanes":[{"name":"The client","sub":"the end customer you bill"},{"name":"AP & Payroll","sub":"pays people and suppliers"},{"name":"Your sub-vendor","sub":"its name is yours to keep"},{"name":"Candidate","sub":"a sub’s person, or your own W2"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"File the week","sub":"your own hours","lane":"Candidate"},{"n":2,"title":"Expense","sub":"receipt attached","lane":"Candidate"},{"n":3,"title":"Timesheet receipt","sub":"the goods receipt, here","lane":"The client"},{"n":4,"title":"Silence counts?","sub":"if the order says so","lane":"The client"},{"n":5,"title":"Pass-through","sub":"every rung, same hours","lane":"Your sub-vendor"},{"n":6,"title":"Checked vs contract","sub":"over hours · past end","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":7,"title":"Employer acceptance","sub":"what we will pay for","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":8,"title":"Milestone accepted","sub":"a receipt of another shape","lane":"The client"}],"refusals":[{"text":"AR cannot accept hours for pay","lane":"AP & Payroll","station":7}],"caption":"The goods receipt of a staffing firm is the signed week. SAP calls it a service entry sheet; the founder named it a timesheet receipt, and the screens use his word. Two signatures from two companies, one row of hours, never one per hop.","short":"Work to approve","page":9,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Timesheet","sap":"a time sheet","note":"The worker files their own week; the agency may enter on their behalf, nobody may sign for them."},{"etyme":"Timesheet receipt — client approval","sap":"the service entry sheet — the goods receipt for services","note":"Same object. “Our goods receipt equivalent is timesheet receipt or expense receipt.” The trade’s word wins on the screen."},{"etyme":"Employer acceptance","sap":"releasing the time sheet for pay","note":"SAP has one approval. Etyme has two signatures, because the client says the work happened and the employer says what it will pay for — different statements."},{"etyme":"Pass-through","sap":"tiered approval","note":"Each rung between the client and the worker sees the same hours it will bill and be billed for."},{"etyme":"Expense receipt","sap":"an expense report","note":"An approved, client-billable expense rides the next bill as a line of its own."},{"etyme":"Milestone receipt","sap":"a milestone on a billing plan","note":"Acceptance is the receipt; it bills as a milestone line."},{"etyme":"Auto-approval","sap":"an approval rule","note":"Read off the order: “silence counts” with a window. It fired for the first time on 2026-09-17, because no order row had ever existed to carry the flag."},{"etyme":"A week checked against its contract","sap":"—","note":"Over the role’s hours or past the last day says so in a sentence before anybody signs; “Approve anyway” takes a reason."}],"png":"img/model/prime-p9.png","sentences":14},{"code":"L1.4","name":"Approve to invoice","lanes":[{"name":"The client","sub":"the end customer you bill"},{"name":"Accounts Receivable","sub":"bills the customer"},{"name":"Account Manager","sub":"sells upward"},{"name":"Finance / Owner","sub":"reads margin and P&L"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Raise the bill","sub":"from the sell line","lane":"Accounts Receivable"},{"n":2,"title":"Four partners","sub":"sold-to · bill-to · ship-to · payer","lane":"Accounts Receivable"},{"n":3,"title":"Tax","sub":"regime · place of supply","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":4,"title":"Receives","sub":"receipt starts the clock","lane":"The client"},{"n":5,"title":"Pays what matched","sub":"never an unmatched bill","lane":"The client"},{"n":6,"title":"Cash application","sub":"a short payment is a question","lane":"Accounts Receivable"},{"n":7,"title":"Age & dun","sub":"from the due date, not period end","lane":"Accounts Receivable"},{"n":8,"title":"Dispute → credit note","sub":"reverses revenue","lane":"Account Manager"},{"n":9,"title":"Exposure & limit","sub":"unpaid + unbilled + committed","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":10,"title":"Collections","sub":"stop-work · write-off","lane":"Finance / Owner"}],"refusals":[{"text":"the payroll desk cannot raise a bill","lane":"Accounts Receivable","station":1}],"caption":"The firm bills its customer — SAP’s process is literally called billing, and the founder’s word matches it. The due date belongs to the document, counted from the day the client received it; nothing schedules one on the calendar to disagree with it.","short":"Approve to invoice","page":11,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Bill","sap":"billing — a billing document, a customer invoice","note":"Aligned by decision: “companies bill (also called invoice) a customer.”"},{"etyme":"Bill line — hours · expense · milestone","sap":"a billing item","note":"Three receipts, three kinds of line, one match."},{"etyme":"Sold-to · bill-to · ship-to · payer","sap":"the four partner roles on a sales document","note":"Identical concept. The first thing a large enterprise asks for."},{"etyme":"Tax","sap":"a tax code with a place of supply","note":"Regime, outcome and place of supply as queryable fields — a return cannot be filed from a blob."},{"etyme":"Cash application","sap":"an incoming payment · a lockbox","note":"A part payment is chased for the balance; a short payment is a question for a person, not arrears."},{"etyme":"Aging","sap":"customer open items","note":"Aged from the day each bill fell due, so sixty-day terms are not late on day forty-five."},{"etyme":"Dunning","sap":"a dunning run","note":"The ladder; who owns each step is a desk."},{"etyme":"Credit note","sap":"a credit memo","note":"A customer document we issue; it reverses revenue. Posted into the bill’s own period."},{"etyme":"Exposure · limit","sap":"credit management","note":"Exposure is unpaid plus delivered-not-billed plus committed for the rest of every running assignment — which is why a client owing a little can be the riskiest name on the list."}],"png":"img/model/prime-p11.png","sentences":18},{"code":"L1.5","name":"Approve to pay","lanes":[{"name":"Your sub-vendor","sub":"its name is yours to keep"},{"name":"AP & Payroll","sub":"pays people and suppliers"},{"name":"Finance / Owner","sub":"reads margin and P&L"},{"name":"Candidate","sub":"a sub’s person, or your own W2"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Issues its invoice","sub":"their number, not ours","lane":"Your sub-vendor"},{"n":2,"title":"Invoice receipt","sub":"received, never raised","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":3,"title":"Three-way match","sub":"order ↔ receipt ↔ invoice","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":4,"title":"Exception → desk","sub":"a decision, with a reason","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":5,"title":"Payment run","sub":"approver is not the raiser","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":6,"title":"Remittance","sub":"what was paid, for what","lane":"Your sub-vendor"},{"n":7,"title":"Payroll","sub":"on accepted hours only","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":8,"title":"Paid","sub":"own pay · never the bill rate","lane":"Candidate"},{"n":9,"title":"Tax data → bureau","sub":"1099 · W-2 data","lane":"Finance / Owner"}],"refusals":[{"text":"receiving it never needs the right to issue one","lane":"AP & Payroll","station":2},{"text":"AR cannot run payroll","lane":"AP & Payroll","station":7}],"caption":"Money out in two directions, two words. A supplier’s invoice is received and matched — the invoice-receipt step. An employee is paid by payroll, which Fieldglass never touches because it stops at the supplier. The candidate sees what they are paid and never what a firm above them charges.","short":"Approve to pay","page":13,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Invoice receipt","sap":"invoice verification — the supplier’s invoice, received and matched","note":"The founder’s term is SAP’s term. The supplier issues the document; we receive it. Receiving it cannot need the permission to issue one of ours."},{"etyme":"Three-way match","sap":"order ↔ goods receipt ↔ invoice receipt","note":"Identical. Work order ↔ timesheet receipt ↔ supplier invoice. A client pays what came through the match."},{"etyme":"Match exception → the AP desk","sap":"a blocked invoice, released by a person","note":"A bill that did not match is a decision, with a reason recorded."},{"etyme":"Payment run","sap":"the automatic payment run","note":"An approver who is not the raiser."},{"etyme":"Remittance","sap":"a payment advice","note":""},{"etyme":"Payroll","sap":"payroll","note":"Fieldglass does not pay workers; it stops at the supplier. Payroll is the supplier’s own system."},{"etyme":"Pay model","sap":"wage types","note":"Salary, hourly, C2C, commission — applied per line."},{"etyme":"Bench reserve","sap":"—","note":"No SAP word. A firm holding back against bench time between projects."},{"etyme":"1099 · W-2 data","sap":"withholding and year-end reporting","note":"Data for the bureau, not the filing."},{"etyme":"Pay day shifts back; bill day shifts forward","sap":"a factory calendar · payment terms","note":"Per company, per category — before, after or neither — decided 2026-09-17 and wired into the dates the same day."}],"png":"img/model/prime-p13.png","sentences":28},{"code":"L1.3 → L1.5","name":"An expense, from receipt to reimbursement","lanes":[{"name":"The client","sub":"the end customer you bill"},{"name":"Account Manager","sub":"sells upward"},{"name":"Accounts Receivable","sub":"bills the customer"},{"name":"AP & Payroll","sub":"pays people and suppliers"},{"name":"Your sub-vendor","sub":"its name is yours to keep"},{"name":"Candidate","sub":"a sub’s person, or your own W2"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Files an expense","sub":"amount · category · receipt","lane":"Candidate"},{"n":2,"title":"Billable to the client?","sub":"the order says; within the ceiling","lane":"Account Manager"},{"n":3,"title":"Approves · or refuses","sub":"a reason travels with a refusal","lane":"The client"},{"n":4,"title":"Told the outcome","sub":"on their own channel","lane":"Candidate"},{"n":5,"title":"Pass-through","sub":"a sub’s person: same expense, every rung","lane":"Your sub-vendor"},{"n":6,"title":"Rides the next bill","sub":"an expense line of its own","lane":"Accounts Receivable"},{"n":7,"title":"Receives · matches","sub":"the approved expense is the receipt","lane":"The client"},{"n":8,"title":"Pays what matched","sub":"PAID with the bill","lane":"The client"},{"n":9,"title":"Reimburses the person","sub":"payroll, or the sub’s invoice","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":10,"title":"Its invoice carries it","sub":"received and matched, one rung down","lane":"Your sub-vendor"},{"n":11,"title":"Reimbursed","sub":"their own money back","lane":"Candidate"}],"refusals":[{"text":"an unapproved expense never bills","lane":"Accounts Receivable","station":6},{"text":"AR cannot pay people","lane":"AP & Payroll","station":9}],"caption":"An expense is the second kind of receipt. The person files it with the paper behind it; the customer approves it or refuses it with a reason that travels with the record; an approved, client-billable expense rides the next bill as a line of its own, and the three-way match takes the approved expense as the receipt — an expense nobody approved never reaches a bill. It is paid with the bill, and reimbursed by whoever pays the person: payroll for an employee, the sub-vendor’s own invoice where a sub is below.","short":"Expenses","page":15,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Expense","sap":"an expense report · a trip","note":"Filed by the person against the placement, with the receipt attached. Nobody else may file it."},{"etyme":"Expense receipt — the customer’s approval","sap":"an approved expense report","note":"The founder’s word: “our goods receipt equivalent is timesheet receipt or expense receipt.” The approval is the receipt."},{"etyme":"Refusal, with a reason","sap":"a rejected expense item","note":"The reason travels with the record and reaches the person on their own channel."},{"etyme":"Expense line on the bill","sap":"a billing item for expenses · re-billing","note":"Rides the next bill as a line of its own, beside the hours lines, and is PAID with it."},{"etyme":"Match: line ↔ approved expense","sap":"the three-way match, receipt-side","note":"Order ↔ approved expense ↔ bill line. An expense nobody approved never bills."},{"etyme":"Reimbursement","sap":"payroll or the vendor’s invoice","note":"Whoever pays the person reimburses them: payroll for an employee; a sub-vendor’s own invoice carries it one rung down."},{"etyme":"Client-billable or not · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/status-ledger.test.ts the ledger: one placement, every table, every station › a flight Tariq paid for: expense DRAFT, SUBMITTED, APPROVED","sap":"a cost assignment on the item the invoice: ISSUED on raising with the expense on it as INVOICED, SUBMITTED on sending, and the invoice-to-raise cycle is done","note":"Read off the order the placement is a line on; a non-billable expense stops at the employer and never reaches the customer. the payment: invoice PAID with its expense, and a payment row saying who paid whom"}],"png":"img/model/prime-p15.png","sentences":4},{"code":"L1.6","name":"Record to report","lanes":[{"name":"Accounts Receivable","sub":"bills the customer"},{"name":"AP & Payroll","sub":"pays people and suppliers"},{"name":"Finance / Owner","sub":"reads margin and P&L"},{"name":"ERP","sub":"the books"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Bill posted","sub":"receivable · revenue","lane":"Accounts Receivable"},{"n":2,"title":"Receipt posted","sub":"cost · payable","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":3,"title":"Payroll posted","sub":"pay · burden","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":4,"title":"Journal","sub":"one balanced entry each","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":5,"title":"Master contract","sub":"optional tag · the roll-up","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":6,"title":"Profitability","sub":"margin, by the deal","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":7,"title":"Earned vs cash","sub":"days to get paid, real months","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":8,"title":"Account map","sub":"our words → their accounts","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":9,"title":"Outbound posting","sub":"to the books they keep","lane":"ERP"},{"n":10,"title":"Reconciliation","sub":"read back, differences owned","lane":"ERP"}],"refusals":[{"text":"the account manager cannot read P&L","lane":"Finance / Owner","station":6}],"caption":"Etyme posts into the books; it does not replace them. The mapping is stated once at the boundary: QuickBooks and Xero say Invoice for the customer document and Bill for the received one — their Invoice is our bill, their Bill is our invoice receipt.","short":"Record to report","page":17,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Journal","sap":"the general ledger · a universal journal","note":"Every posting turns into a balanced entry; the receivable move on every bill and the cash move on every applied receipt."},{"etyme":"The pair — a sell line and the buy line that funds it","sap":"a sales item and a purchase item settled to one cost object","note":"A placement’s own margin. Always written by the award, because a buy line pays for some sell line."},{"etyme":"Master contract — the profitability roll-up","sap":"an internal order · a work-breakdown element","note":"The Etyme-2017 word, kept: the container that once held both sides on one row is now an optional tag. A company tags sell and buy lines to one when it wants to see the deal’s margin. Not a commercial document; nobody signs one — same in SAP, where the sales order and the purchase order both settle to it."},{"etyme":"Profitability by pair, person, customer, master","sap":"margin analysis","note":"Read from real revenue and cost; gated on the right to read P&L, which the account manager deliberately does not hold."},{"etyme":"Earned against cash","sap":"revenue recognition","note":"Days to get paid counted back through real months rather than divided by an average, so growth does not move it."},{"etyme":"Currency","sap":"currency types and exchange rates","note":"Money in minor units, always."},{"etyme":"ERP account map","sap":"the chart of accounts · an integration","note":"Businesses pay for QuickBooks, SAP and NetSuite directly; Etyme posts to them."},{"etyme":"Reconciliation · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/full-spine.test.ts","sap":"clearing · a bank statement","note":"Reads the books back; a difference is a row somebody owns."}],"png":"img/model/prime-p17.png","sentences":18},{"code":"L1.7","name":"Govern and protect","lanes":[{"name":"The client","sub":"the end customer you bill"},{"name":"Compliance Officer","sub":"reads; writes nothing"},{"name":"Finance / Owner","sub":"reads margin and P&L"},{"name":"Etyme, unprompted","sub":"what it does on its own"},{"name":"Your sub-vendor","sub":"its name is yours to keep"},{"name":"Candidate","sub":"a sub’s person, or your own W2"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Tenure ledger","sub":"the person, at the client","lane":"Compliance Officer"},{"n":2,"title":"Days on site","sub":"counted once per day","lane":"The client"},{"n":3,"title":"Classification","sub":"W2 · 1099 · C2C","lane":"Compliance Officer"},{"n":4,"title":"Approval chains","sub":"by rule and by name","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":5,"title":"Segregation","sub":"nobody decides two desks","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":6,"title":"Supplier standing","sub":"probation · approved · preferred","lane":"Compliance Officer"},{"n":7,"title":"Insured · authorized","sub":"the client always sees this","lane":"Your sub-vendor"},{"n":8,"title":"Concentration","sub":"one client, one person","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":9,"title":"Access log","sub":"every read · refusals too","lane":"Etyme, unprompted"},{"n":10,"title":"Automation log","sub":"why · and can it be undone","lane":"Etyme, unprompted"},{"n":11,"title":"Do-not-return list","sub":"the company’s own","lane":"Compliance Officer"},{"n":12,"title":"Told what is held","sub":"own pay only","lane":"Candidate"}],"refusals":[{"text":"never read across companies","lane":"Compliance Officer","station":11},{"text":"nobody signs their own — BLOCK, in a sentence","lane":"Finance / Owner","station":5}],"caption":"The moat, not the wedge: tenure accrues to the person at the client across every supplier, counted once per day on site. SAP records what changed; Etyme also records why, and whether it can be undone — and every read of another person’s data leaves a row, including the refusals.","short":"Govern and protect","page":19,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Tenure — the person at the client, across suppliers","sap":"a tenure policy · contract elements on the person","note":"Fieldglass tracks tenure per worker at the buyer within its own walls. Etyme’s claim is across suppliers who are not all on one system — which is every buyer who cannot afford one."},{"etyme":"Worker classification","sap":"employee group and subgroup","note":"BLOCK where legally grounded."},{"etyme":"Approval chain","sap":"a release strategy · a workflow","note":"Most requisitions must clear without a human. A desk nobody named falls back; it never refuses."},{"etyme":"Segregation of duties","sap":"an access-control ruleset","note":"“You recommended this firm, so the desks decide it without you.” A sentence, never a disabled button."},{"etyme":"Supplier standing","sap":"supplier risk","note":"Probation · approved · preferred, read by the tier rule."},{"etyme":"Concentration","sap":"margin analysis by customer","note":"Revenue share riding on one client, one supplier, one person, with a named risk owner."},{"etyme":"Access log — every read of a person","sap":"an audit log · read-access logging","note":"The nearest thing logs reads of sensitive fields. Etyme logs the refusals too."},{"etyme":"Company walls","sap":"authorization objects · company codes","note":"A caller with no company is refused, never handed every company’s list."},{"etyme":"Automation log — what the system did on its own","sap":"change documents","note":"SAP records what changed. Etyme records the plain-English reason and an honest reversible flag, and every action name is declared on a ladder."},{"etyme":"Do-not-return list","sap":"a vendor block · a rehire flag","note":"Read by every desk that puts people forward; written by the desk that owns who goes forward. Never read across companies."},{"etyme":"Whose rate is on the row","sap":"rate visibility","note":"The person named on a sell line is the subject of it, not a party to it."},{"etyme":"What we tell people about their data · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/desks-in-tandem.test.ts the desks, in tandem: one placement, and at every station the wrong desk is refused › reads what the placement made, and the recruiter — who cannot see what anyone costs — cannot · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/full-spine.test.ts Step 5 — Computer Systems takes it on and asks its sub-vendor › leaves CloudEPA unable to see what Auralis agreed to pay · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/placement-payload.test.ts a client opens a placement bought through two firms › the client is sent nothing at all that names the firm below its supplier the buy contract its supplier signed to staff the job is not in the client’s copy the firm below is not on the client’s copy as a certificate, nor as a verdict about one who put the person in front of the supplier, and what they asked for them, stays with the supplier no figure anywhere in the client’s copy is a rate from below the contract it pays the pay days on the supplier’s own payroll are not on the client’s timeline the client’s owner holds every permission their own company can grant, and still reads none of the supplier’s cost or margin","sap":"information lifecycle · data privacy the owner Step 21 — one placement, opened, top to bottom › as the read the client is still told how many firms stand between it and the person, because that is its own a line is named by the person and the place, and never by a contract id question to answer the client still reads what it is billed, who it pays, and whether the person may start the supplier opening the same placement still sees its own buy leg, so what changed is the side document and not the fields a firm that is not a party is told there is no such placement, rather than that it may not look a placement is a line on a document, and says which › purchase order, and this person as a numbered line of it the supplier billing against the same row reads it as a sales order, because it is not buying anything","note":"A page of their own, off until they turn it on. writes an access log row for the refusal as well the client reads what its own document authorized and what has been billed against it everybody else on the same document is listed with it, because five people on one order is one a seat nobody has papered yet says so in a sentence, and says what will attach a line on no master contract is offered the tag rather than warned about it the firm that raised the paper reads it as its"}],"png":"img/model/prime-p19.png","sentences":67}]},{"meta":{"key":"bench","number":"6","name":"Bench vendor","label":"Bench vendor","tagline":"Owns a bench of people who consented to be sold. Sells them up, keeps them warm between.","position":"A business model more than a position: the firm whose asset is its bench. It attracts people nobody else can find in a niche skill, keeps them warm between assignments, and sells them on evidence rather than a forwarded CV — to a prime, or straight to a client. Every person on it granted a listing, and can take it back.","desks":["Owner","Admin","Recruiter","Resource Manager","Account Manager","HR","Contract Manager","Accounts Receivable","AP & Payroll","Finance","Compliance Officer"],"doors":["CloudEPA /demo · world-cloudepa"],"how":"","summary":"The supplier drawing without a rung below it: a bench vendor buys from its own people. What is heaviest here is the bottom lane — consent to be represented, the check-ins, releasing-soon and rolloff, the person’s own page — and the rule that bench burn is the vendor’s risk to watch. Etyme itself runs no bench and places nobody; the moment it competed with its own suppliers the network would stop growing. Shaded lane — a party outside the firm. Anything crossing into it is a document a counterparty reads. Blue-edged lane — one of this party’s own desks. Its boxes are solid; everyone else’s are faded but still there, because the stream does not change — only who is looking. Labelled arrow — the artifact that moves: requisition, submission, order, timesheet receipt, bill, invoice. Dashed box — a station the operating model names that the build does not yet do as a moment of its own. Clay ma"},"streams":[{"code":"L1.1","name":"Source to contract","lanes":[{"name":"Who you sell to","sub":"a prime, or the client"},{"name":"Account Manager","sub":"sells upward"},{"name":"Recruiter","sub":"procures profiles"},{"name":"Your bench","sub":"the listing is theirs"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Raise requisition","sub":"the role, the months, the rate","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":2,"title":"Three desks clear it","sub":"HR · Procurement · the lead","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":3,"title":"Release to suppliers","sub":"the ones Procurement cleared","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":4,"title":"Accept · pass down","sub":"a band of its own","lane":"Account Manager"},{"n":5,"title":"Source & match","sub":"a score says why","lane":"Recruiter"},{"n":6,"title":"Consent to represent","sub":"the listing — yours to give","lane":"Your bench"},{"n":7,"title":"Submit","sub":"a rate, at this rung","lane":"Recruiter"},{"n":8,"title":"Shortlist · negotiate","sub":"right-to-work first","lane":"Account Manager"},{"n":9,"title":"Interview","sub":"rounds in turn","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":10,"title":"Award","sub":"the order and its first line","lane":"Who you sell to"}],"refusals":[{"text":"no listing, no submission — unless own W2","lane":"Recruiter","station":7}],"caption":"One requisition becomes one award. It clears three desks first — HR reads the role, Procurement audits the suppliers, the lead who owns the cost center signs the money — and nobody signs their own; within plan every desk clears by rule and it publishes itself. Every arrow that crosses into a shaded lane is a document a counterparty reads — and the rate band travels on the invitation, never on the requisition, so no supplier reads another’s.","short":"Source to contract","page":2,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Requisition","sap":"a purchase requisition · a job posting","note":"Same object. Etyme clears it through three desks — HR reads the role, Procurement audits the suppliers, the cost-center lead signs the money; SAP puts a release strategy on it."},{"etyme":"Rate band","sap":"a rate guideline · a price on the vendor record","note":"Both keep the price per supplier where no other supplier can read it. Etyme puts it on the invitation."},{"etyme":"Supplier release","sap":"a request for quotation to the source list","note":"“These vendors may quote.” The program office decides, never the hiring manager."},{"etyme":"Bench listing — consent to be marketed","sap":"—","note":"No SAP word. Fieldglass has a worker profile; nobody in SAP consents to be sold. The invariant with no counterpart."},{"etyme":"Submission","sap":"a quotation · a job-seeker submittal","note":"A quotation at a rate, one per rung of the chain — two rows, one chain."},{"etyme":"Interview","sap":"an interview","note":"Only whoever is hiring may set up or decide a round."},{"etyme":"Award","sap":"creating the purchase order · creating the work order","note":"In SAP the award *is* the order. Etyme’s award now raises the order and writes the contract as its first line."},{"etyme":"Requirement going down a chain · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/ask-for-person.test.ts asking for a person you were shown › a candidate who was submitted and not hired is on the register with everything the client knows, and the read leaves a trail","sap":"a tiered supplier · subcontracting somebody never put in front of this client cannot be opened, and the refusal is logged too","note":"The prime retypes the role for its sub under a band of its own; the sub never learns the end client unless the agreement requires disclosure. asking for him on a published role goes to the supplier on the thread for that role, and says so"}],"png":"img/model/bench-p2.png","sentences":47},{"code":"L1.2","name":"Contract to onboard","lanes":[{"name":"Who you sell to","sub":"a prime, or the client"},{"name":"Account Manager","sub":"sells upward"},{"name":"Contract Manager","sub":"papers it"},{"name":"HR","sub":"candidate & supplier standing"},{"name":"Your bench","sub":"the listing is theirs"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Agreement, if new","sub":"both sign · optional","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":2,"title":"Countersign","sub":"the later date counts","lane":"Account Manager"},{"n":3,"title":"Purchase order","sub":"the header · a ceiling","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":4,"title":"Sell line","sub":"this person, this rate","lane":"Contract Manager"},{"n":5,"title":"Buy line","sub":"pays the sub, or payroll","lane":"Contract Manager"},{"n":6,"title":"Own W2 — no order","sub":"employment is the paper","lane":"Your bench"},{"n":7,"title":"Candidate green","sub":"I-9 · check · license","lane":"HR"},{"n":8,"title":"Papers","sub":"a link · no sign-in","lane":"Your bench"},{"n":9,"title":"Company green","sub":"insurance · terms","lane":"HR"},{"n":10,"title":"Activate","sub":"both lines move","lane":"Contract Manager"},{"n":11,"title":"Start date announced","sub":"not yet a moment","lane":"Who you sell to"}],"refusals":[{"text":"no I-9, no start · lapsed cover blocks","lane":"Contract Manager","station":10}],"caption":"Two gates, not one: the candidate is green and the company is green. The buy line forks — an order to a sub-vendor carries a ceiling; an employment to your own W2 carries no order at all, because you do not raise a purchase order to your own employee.","short":"Contract to onboard","page":4,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Agreement · MSA","sap":"an outline agreement · a sales contract","note":"Optional since 2026-09-18. Both signatures, and the date that matters is the later one. SAP has no countersignature of its own; that lives in a contracts tool. Never “master agreement” on a screen — “master contract” is the profitability roll-up, a different thing."},{"etyme":"Purchase order · sales order · work order","sap":"one order, mirrored: a PO on the buyer, a sales order on the seller","note":"One row, three names. The header: counterparty, ceiling, dates, terms, the four partner roles."},{"etyme":"Sell line — bills the customer","sap":"a sales-order item, one per worker","note":"A line on the order: this person, this rate, this site. What the firm bills from."},{"etyme":"Buy line to a sub-vendor — pays by invoice receipt","sap":"a service item on our order to the vendor","note":"Draws down our order to the sub. Rhythm and terms read from the document; the dates are the line’s own, because a line is a person."},{"etyme":"Buy line to own W2 — pays by payroll","sap":"a hiring action, not a vendor record","note":"No order to your own employee. SAP files the person under HR, never under purchasing."},{"etyme":"Supplier onboarding — four desks","sap":"supplier registration and qualification","note":"Etyme walks department lead, Procurement, HR and Finance in order, each verifying only its own items."},{"etyme":"Work authorization · I-9","sap":"a residence-status record on the person","note":"BLOCK. The form has an edition; an I-9 with nothing behind it is not held."},{"etyme":"Certificate of insurance","sap":"a supplier certificate with a validity window","note":"Etyme reads the start date as a floor — cover beginning next month does not cover somebody starting this week."},{"etyme":"Compliance · Agreement · Proof","sap":"—","note":"Etyme’s three purposes decide behavior. SAP scatters them across HR, procurement and document management."},{"etyme":"Activate · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/cover-chase.test.ts a supplier whose cover has not begun is chased for the weeks nobody is insured › chase names the supplier whose cover starts next month, and says how long nobody is insured and it asks that supplier for the certificate, instead of treating the policy that starts later as on file clear · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/credential-renewal.test.ts the nightly chase asking a nurse for her renewal › asks her for the renewal without anybody typing it into the seed asks the firm that places her to do the asking, and never the client she works at tells her why she is being asked, in a sentence that names her board and the days she has left","sap":"the hire · the release the nightly and the automation log says in plain English why it asked, and that cancelling undoes it the placement thread reads the sub-vendor’s cover as not started yet, rather than as the stored sends the ask to her own address, so the link is hers rather than her agency’s writes down that it did this by itself, why, and that cancelling the request undoes it tells her by email as well, because a license running out is worth leaving the app for","note":"Both lines move together. Payment terms are not yet a gate. and the thread says the firm below cannot put anybody forward, in the same words the submission door uses and the moment the cover has begun the same thread reads it as in force, and nobody is chased reads her license as the one thing worth chasing tonight, and says so in the third person to the desk does not ask her twice when it runs again the next night says nothing about a consultant who holds no license, which is an answer rather than a gap"}],"png":"img/model/bench-p4.png","sentences":17},{"code":"L1.3","name":"Work to approve","lanes":[{"name":"Who you sell to","sub":"a prime, or the client"},{"name":"AP & Payroll","sub":"pays people and suppliers"},{"name":"Your bench","sub":"the listing is theirs"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"File the week","sub":"your own hours","lane":"Your bench"},{"n":2,"title":"Expense","sub":"receipt attached","lane":"Your bench"},{"n":3,"title":"Timesheet receipt","sub":"the goods receipt, here","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":4,"title":"Silence counts?","sub":"if the order says so","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":5,"title":"Checked vs contract","sub":"over hours · past end","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":6,"title":"Employer acceptance","sub":"what we will pay for","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":7,"title":"Milestone accepted","sub":"a receipt of another shape","lane":"Who you sell to"}],"refusals":[{"text":"AR cannot accept hours for pay","lane":"AP & Payroll","station":6}],"caption":"The goods receipt of a staffing firm is the signed week. SAP calls it a service entry sheet; the founder named it a timesheet receipt, and the screens use his word. Two signatures from two companies, one row of hours, never one per hop.","short":"Work to approve","page":6,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Timesheet","sap":"a time sheet","note":"The worker files their own week; the agency may enter on their behalf, nobody may sign for them."},{"etyme":"Timesheet receipt — client approval","sap":"the service entry sheet — the goods receipt for services","note":"Same object. “Our goods receipt equivalent is timesheet receipt or expense receipt.” The trade’s word wins on the screen."},{"etyme":"Employer acceptance","sap":"releasing the time sheet for pay","note":"SAP has one approval. Etyme has two signatures, because the client says the work happened and the employer says what it will pay for — different statements."},{"etyme":"Pass-through","sap":"tiered approval","note":"Each rung between the client and the worker sees the same hours it will bill and be billed for."},{"etyme":"Expense receipt","sap":"an expense report","note":"An approved, client-billable expense rides the next bill as a line of its own."},{"etyme":"Milestone receipt","sap":"a milestone on a billing plan","note":"Acceptance is the receipt; it bills as a milestone line."},{"etyme":"Auto-approval","sap":"an approval rule","note":"Read off the order: “silence counts” with a window. It fired for the first time on 2026-09-17, because no order row had ever existed to carry the flag."},{"etyme":"A week checked against its contract","sap":"—","note":"Over the role’s hours or past the last day says so in a sentence before anybody signs; “Approve anyway” takes a reason."}],"png":"img/model/bench-p6.png","sentences":0},{"code":"L1.4","name":"Approve to invoice","lanes":[{"name":"Who you sell to","sub":"a prime, or the client"},{"name":"Accounts Receivable","sub":"bills the customer"},{"name":"Account Manager","sub":"sells upward"},{"name":"Finance / Owner","sub":"reads margin and P&L"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Raise the bill","sub":"from the sell line","lane":"Accounts Receivable"},{"n":2,"title":"Four partners","sub":"sold-to · bill-to · ship-to · payer","lane":"Accounts Receivable"},{"n":3,"title":"Tax","sub":"regime · place of supply","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":4,"title":"Receives","sub":"receipt starts the clock","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":5,"title":"Pays what matched","sub":"never an unmatched bill","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":6,"title":"Cash application","sub":"a short payment is a question","lane":"Accounts Receivable"},{"n":7,"title":"Age & dun","sub":"from the due date, not period end","lane":"Accounts Receivable"},{"n":8,"title":"Dispute → credit note","sub":"reverses revenue","lane":"Account Manager"},{"n":9,"title":"Exposure & limit","sub":"unpaid + unbilled + committed","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":10,"title":"Collections","sub":"stop-work · write-off","lane":"Finance / Owner"}],"refusals":[{"text":"the payroll desk cannot raise a bill","lane":"Accounts Receivable","station":1}],"caption":"The firm bills its customer — SAP’s process is literally called billing, and the founder’s word matches it. The due date belongs to the document, counted from the day the client received it; nothing schedules one on the calendar to disagree with it.","short":"Approve to invoice","page":7,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Bill","sap":"billing — a billing document, a customer invoice","note":"Aligned by decision: “companies bill (also called invoice) a customer.”"},{"etyme":"Bill line — hours · expense · milestone","sap":"a billing item","note":"Three receipts, three kinds of line, one match."},{"etyme":"Sold-to · bill-to · ship-to · payer","sap":"the four partner roles on a sales document","note":"Identical concept. The first thing a large enterprise asks for."},{"etyme":"Tax","sap":"a tax code with a place of supply","note":"Regime, outcome and place of supply as queryable fields — a return cannot be filed from a blob."},{"etyme":"Cash application","sap":"an incoming payment · a lockbox","note":"A part payment is chased for the balance; a short payment is a question for a person, not arrears."},{"etyme":"Aging","sap":"customer open items","note":"Aged from the day each bill fell due, so sixty-day terms are not late on day forty-five."},{"etyme":"Dunning","sap":"a dunning run","note":"The ladder; who owns each step is a desk."},{"etyme":"Credit note","sap":"a credit memo","note":"A customer document we issue; it reverses revenue. Posted into the bill’s own period."},{"etyme":"Exposure · limit","sap":"credit management","note":"Exposure is unpaid plus delivered-not-billed plus committed for the rest of every running assignment — which is why a client owing a little can be the riskiest name on the list."}],"png":"img/model/bench-p7.png","sentences":0},{"code":"L1.5","name":"Approve to pay","lanes":[{"name":"AP & Payroll","sub":"pays people and suppliers"},{"name":"Finance / Owner","sub":"reads margin and P&L"},{"name":"Your bench","sub":"the listing is theirs"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Invoice receipt","sub":"received, never raised","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":2,"title":"Three-way match","sub":"order ↔ receipt ↔ invoice","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":3,"title":"Exception → desk","sub":"a decision, with a reason","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":4,"title":"Payment run","sub":"approver is not the raiser","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":5,"title":"Payroll","sub":"on accepted hours only","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":6,"title":"Paid","sub":"own pay · never the bill rate","lane":"Your bench"},{"n":7,"title":"Tax data → bureau","sub":"1099 · W-2 data","lane":"Finance / Owner"}],"refusals":[{"text":"receiving it never needs the right to issue one","lane":"AP & Payroll","station":1},{"text":"AR cannot run payroll","lane":"AP & Payroll","station":5}],"caption":"Money out in two directions, two words. A supplier’s invoice is received and matched — the invoice-receipt step. An employee is paid by payroll, which Fieldglass never touches because it stops at the supplier. The candidate sees what they are paid and never what a firm above them charges.","short":"Approve to pay","page":8,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Invoice receipt","sap":"invoice verification — the supplier’s invoice, received and matched","note":"The founder’s term is SAP’s term. The supplier issues the document; we receive it. Receiving it cannot need the permission to issue one of ours."},{"etyme":"Three-way match","sap":"order ↔ goods receipt ↔ invoice receipt","note":"Identical. Work order ↔ timesheet receipt ↔ supplier invoice. A client pays what came through the match."},{"etyme":"Match exception → the AP desk","sap":"a blocked invoice, released by a person","note":"A bill that did not match is a decision, with a reason recorded."},{"etyme":"Payment run","sap":"the automatic payment run","note":"An approver who is not the raiser."},{"etyme":"Remittance","sap":"a payment advice","note":""},{"etyme":"Payroll","sap":"payroll","note":"Fieldglass does not pay workers; it stops at the supplier. Payroll is the supplier’s own system."},{"etyme":"Pay model","sap":"wage types","note":"Salary, hourly, C2C, commission — applied per line."},{"etyme":"Bench reserve","sap":"—","note":"No SAP word. A firm holding back against bench time between projects."},{"etyme":"1099 · W-2 data","sap":"withholding and year-end reporting","note":"Data for the bureau, not the filing."},{"etyme":"Pay day shifts back; bill day shifts forward","sap":"a factory calendar · payment terms","note":"Per company, per category — before, after or neither — decided 2026-09-17 and wired into the dates the same day."}],"png":"img/model/bench-p8.png","sentences":0},{"code":"L1.3 → L1.5","name":"An expense, from receipt to reimbursement","lanes":[{"name":"Who you sell to","sub":"a prime, or the client"},{"name":"Account Manager","sub":"sells upward"},{"name":"Accounts Receivable","sub":"bills the customer"},{"name":"AP & Payroll","sub":"pays people and suppliers"},{"name":"Your bench","sub":"the listing is theirs"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Files an expense","sub":"amount · category · receipt","lane":"Your bench"},{"n":2,"title":"Billable to the client?","sub":"the order says; within the ceiling","lane":"Account Manager"},{"n":3,"title":"Approves · or refuses","sub":"a reason travels with a refusal","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":4,"title":"Told the outcome","sub":"on their own channel","lane":"Your bench"},{"n":5,"title":"Rides the next bill","sub":"an expense line of its own","lane":"Accounts Receivable"},{"n":6,"title":"Receives · matches","sub":"the approved expense is the receipt","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":7,"title":"Pays what matched","sub":"PAID with the bill","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":8,"title":"Reimburses the person","sub":"payroll, or the sub’s invoice","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":9,"title":"Reimbursed","sub":"their own money back","lane":"Your bench"}],"refusals":[{"text":"an unapproved expense never bills","lane":"Accounts Receivable","station":5},{"text":"AR cannot pay people","lane":"AP & Payroll","station":8}],"caption":"An expense is the second kind of receipt. The person files it with the paper behind it; the customer approves it or refuses it with a reason that travels with the record; an approved, client-billable expense rides the next bill as a line of its own, and the three-way match takes the approved expense as the receipt — an expense nobody approved never reaches a bill. It is paid with the bill, and reimbursed by whoever pays the person: payroll for an employee, the sub-vendor’s own invoice where a sub is below.","short":"Expenses","page":9,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Expense","sap":"an expense report · a trip","note":"Filed by the person against the placement, with the receipt attached. Nobody else may file it."},{"etyme":"Expense receipt — the customer’s approval","sap":"an approved expense report","note":"The founder’s word: “our goods receipt equivalent is timesheet receipt or expense receipt.” The approval is the receipt."},{"etyme":"Refusal, with a reason","sap":"a rejected expense item","note":"The reason travels with the record and reaches the person on their own channel."},{"etyme":"Expense line on the bill","sap":"a billing item for expenses · re-billing","note":"Rides the next bill as a line of its own, beside the hours lines, and is PAID with it."},{"etyme":"Match: line ↔ approved expense","sap":"the three-way match, receipt-side","note":"Order ↔ approved expense ↔ bill line. An expense nobody approved never bills."},{"etyme":"Reimbursement","sap":"payroll or the vendor’s invoice","note":"Whoever pays the person reimburses them: payroll for an employee; a sub-vendor’s own invoice carries it one rung down."},{"etyme":"Client-billable or not","sap":"a cost assignment on the item","note":"Read off the order the placement is a line on; a non-billable expense stops at the employer and never reaches the customer."}],"png":"img/model/bench-p9.png","sentences":0},{"code":"L1.6","name":"Record to report","lanes":[{"name":"Accounts Receivable","sub":"bills the customer"},{"name":"AP & Payroll","sub":"pays people and suppliers"},{"name":"Finance / Owner","sub":"reads margin and P&L"},{"name":"ERP","sub":"the books"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Bill posted","sub":"receivable · revenue","lane":"Accounts Receivable"},{"n":2,"title":"Receipt posted","sub":"cost · payable","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":3,"title":"Payroll posted","sub":"pay · burden","lane":"AP & Payroll"},{"n":4,"title":"Journal","sub":"one balanced entry each","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":5,"title":"Master contract","sub":"optional tag · the roll-up","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":6,"title":"Profitability","sub":"margin, by the deal","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":7,"title":"Earned vs cash","sub":"days to get paid, real months","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":8,"title":"Account map","sub":"our words → their accounts","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":9,"title":"Outbound posting","sub":"to the books they keep","lane":"ERP"},{"n":10,"title":"Reconciliation","sub":"read back, differences owned","lane":"ERP"}],"refusals":[{"text":"the account manager cannot read P&L","lane":"Finance / Owner","station":6}],"caption":"Etyme posts into the books; it does not replace them. The mapping is stated once at the boundary: QuickBooks and Xero say Invoice for the customer document and Bill for the received one — their Invoice is our bill, their Bill is our invoice receipt.","short":"Record to report","page":10,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Journal","sap":"the general ledger · a universal journal","note":"Every posting turns into a balanced entry; the receivable move on every bill and the cash move on every applied receipt."},{"etyme":"The pair — a sell line and the buy line that funds it","sap":"a sales item and a purchase item settled to one cost object","note":"A placement’s own margin. Always written by the award, because a buy line pays for some sell line."},{"etyme":"Master contract — the profitability roll-up","sap":"an internal order · a work-breakdown element","note":"The Etyme-2017 word, kept: the container that once held both sides on one row is now an optional tag. A company tags sell and buy lines to one when it wants to see the deal’s margin. Not a commercial document; nobody signs one — same in SAP, where the sales order and the purchase order both settle to it."},{"etyme":"Profitability by pair, person, customer, master","sap":"margin analysis","note":"Read from real revenue and cost; gated on the right to read P&L, which the account manager deliberately does not hold."},{"etyme":"Earned against cash","sap":"revenue recognition","note":"Days to get paid counted back through real months rather than divided by an average, so growth does not move it."},{"etyme":"Currency","sap":"currency types and exchange rates","note":"Money in minor units, always."},{"etyme":"ERP account map","sap":"the chart of accounts · an integration","note":"Businesses pay for QuickBooks, SAP and NetSuite directly; Etyme posts to them."},{"etyme":"Reconciliation","sap":"clearing · a bank statement","note":"Reads the books back; a difference is a row somebody owns."}],"png":"img/model/bench-p10.png","sentences":0},{"code":"L1.7","name":"Govern and protect","lanes":[{"name":"Who you sell to","sub":"a prime, or the client"},{"name":"Compliance Officer","sub":"reads; writes nothing"},{"name":"Finance / Owner","sub":"reads margin and P&L"},{"name":"Etyme, unprompted","sub":"what it does on its own"},{"name":"Your bench","sub":"the listing is theirs"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Tenure ledger","sub":"the person, at the client","lane":"Compliance Officer"},{"n":2,"title":"Days on site","sub":"counted once per day","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":3,"title":"Classification","sub":"W2 · 1099 · C2C","lane":"Compliance Officer"},{"n":4,"title":"Approval chains","sub":"by rule and by name","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":5,"title":"Segregation","sub":"nobody decides two desks","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":6,"title":"Supplier standing","sub":"probation · approved · preferred","lane":"Compliance Officer"},{"n":7,"title":"Concentration","sub":"one client, one person","lane":"Finance / Owner"},{"n":8,"title":"Access log","sub":"every read · refusals too","lane":"Etyme, unprompted"},{"n":9,"title":"Automation log","sub":"why · and can it be undone","lane":"Etyme, unprompted"},{"n":10,"title":"Do-not-return list","sub":"the company’s own","lane":"Compliance Officer"},{"n":11,"title":"Told what is held","sub":"own pay only","lane":"Your bench"}],"refusals":[{"text":"never read across companies","lane":"Compliance Officer","station":10},{"text":"nobody signs their own — BLOCK, in a sentence","lane":"Finance / Owner","station":5}],"caption":"The moat, not the wedge: tenure accrues to the person at the client across every supplier, counted once per day on site. SAP records what changed; Etyme also records why, and whether it can be undone — and every read of another person’s data leaves a row, including the refusals.","short":"Govern and protect","page":11,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Tenure — the person at the client, across suppliers","sap":"a tenure policy · contract elements on the person","note":"Fieldglass tracks tenure per worker at the buyer within its own walls. Etyme’s claim is across suppliers who are not all on one system — which is every buyer who cannot afford one."},{"etyme":"Worker classification","sap":"employee group and subgroup","note":"BLOCK where legally grounded."},{"etyme":"Approval chain","sap":"a release strategy · a workflow","note":"Most requisitions must clear without a human. A desk nobody named falls back; it never refuses."},{"etyme":"Segregation of duties","sap":"an access-control ruleset","note":"“You recommended this firm, so the desks decide it without you.” A sentence, never a disabled button."},{"etyme":"Supplier standing","sap":"supplier risk","note":"Probation · approved · preferred, read by the tier rule."},{"etyme":"Concentration","sap":"margin analysis by customer","note":"Revenue share riding on one client, one supplier, one person, with a named risk owner."},{"etyme":"Access log — every read of a person","sap":"an audit log · read-access logging","note":"The nearest thing logs reads of sensitive fields. Etyme logs the refusals too."},{"etyme":"Company walls","sap":"authorization objects · company codes","note":"A caller with no company is refused, never handed every company’s list."},{"etyme":"Automation log — what the system did on its own","sap":"change documents","note":"SAP records what changed. Etyme records the plain-English reason and an honest reversible flag, and every action name is declared on a ladder."},{"etyme":"Do-not-return list","sap":"a vendor block · a rehire flag","note":"Read by every desk that puts people forward; written by the desk that owns who goes forward. Never read across companies."},{"etyme":"Whose rate is on the row","sap":"rate visibility","note":"The person named on a sell line is the subject of it, not a party to it."},{"etyme":"What we tell people about their data · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/standing-and-seats.test.ts standing, units and cold seats › Northbend Athletic rates Pinnacle on probation and Brightmoor preferred, and the suppliers page says so","sap":"information lifecycle · data privacy a word not on the list is refused in a sentence Northbend Athletic adds a Data practice under Technology; adding it twice hands back the first","note":"A page of their own, off until they turn it on. a kind the schema does not name is refused a seat nobody has advertised in eight weeks goes cold overnight; one seen last week stays live"}],"png":"img/model/bench-p11.png","sentences":6}]},{"meta":{"key":"self","number":"7","name":"Self-employed — a consultant’s own corporation","label":"Self-employed","tagline":"One person, two lanes: the firm that sells and insures, and the worker who files and is paid.","position":"A one-person sub-vendor. The corporation sells to a prime or a bench vendor on a sell line, holds its own liability cover and good standing, issues its own invoice, and pays its owner. The owner files the week, is told the start date, and sees only their own pay. The same person appears in the supply lane and the candidate lane, and the two must not be confused: the firm’s insurance can lapse while the person is perfectly authorized.","desks":["Owner — and the person the work is about"],"doors":["Colleen Byrne —","Byrne","Critical","Care","LLC /demo · colleen-byrne"],"how":"","summary":"Colleen Byrne owns Byrne Critical Care LLC. It carries the liability cover her assignment depends on; on 2026-09-17 the seed found she had no seat at her own corporation, so the chase for that cover had no address to go to. That is the shape this party has to get right: a corporation with one seat, a seat with one corporation, and the paperwork of each kept apart. Shaded lane — a party outside the firm. Anything crossing into it is a document a counterparty reads. Blue-edged lane — one of this party’s own desks. Its boxes are solid; everyone else’s are faded but still there, because the stream does not change — only who is looking. Labelled arrow — the artifact that moves: requisition, submission, order, timesheet receipt, bill, invoice. Dashed box — a station the operating model names that the build does not yet do as a moment of its own. Clay mark — a refusal. Segregation of duties is "},"streams":[{"code":"L1.1","name":"Source to contract","lanes":[{"name":"Who you sell to","sub":"prime · bench · client"},{"name":"The firm above you","sub":"its desks, doing the buying"},{"name":"You, as the firm","sub":"sells · insures · invoices"},{"name":"You, as the worker","sub":"files · is cleared · is paid"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Raise requisition","sub":"the role, the months, the rate","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":2,"title":"Three desks clear it","sub":"HR · Procurement · the lead","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":3,"title":"Release to suppliers","sub":"the ones Procurement cleared","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":4,"title":"Accept · pass down","sub":"a band of its own","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":5,"title":"Sub records the role","sub":"its own record of it","lane":"You, as the firm"},{"n":6,"title":"Source & match","sub":"a score says why","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":7,"title":"Consent to represent","sub":"the listing — yours to give","lane":"You, as the worker"},{"n":8,"title":"Submit","sub":"a rate, at this rung","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":9,"title":"Shortlist · negotiate","sub":"right-to-work first","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":10,"title":"Interview","sub":"rounds in turn","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":11,"title":"Award","sub":"the order and its first line","lane":"Who you sell to"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"One requisition becomes one award. It clears three desks first — HR reads the role, Procurement audits the suppliers, the lead who owns the cost center signs the money — and nobody signs their own; within plan every desk clears by rule and it publishes itself. Every arrow that crosses into a shaded lane is a document a counterparty reads — and the rate band travels on the invitation, never on the requisition, so no supplier reads another’s.","short":"Source to contract","page":2,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Requisition","sap":"a purchase requisition · a job posting","note":"Same object. Etyme clears it through three desks — HR reads the role, Procurement audits the suppliers, the cost-center lead signs the money; SAP puts a release strategy on it."},{"etyme":"Rate band","sap":"a rate guideline · a price on the vendor record","note":"Both keep the price per supplier where no other supplier can read it. Etyme puts it on the invitation."},{"etyme":"Supplier release","sap":"a request for quotation to the source list","note":"“These vendors may quote.” The program office decides, never the hiring manager."},{"etyme":"Bench listing — consent to be marketed","sap":"—","note":"No SAP word. Fieldglass has a worker profile; nobody in SAP consents to be sold. The invariant with no counterpart."},{"etyme":"Submission","sap":"a quotation · a job-seeker submittal","note":"A quotation at a rate, one per rung of the chain — two rows, one chain."},{"etyme":"Interview","sap":"an interview","note":"Only whoever is hiring may set up or decide a round."},{"etyme":"Award","sap":"creating the purchase order · creating the work order","note":"In SAP the award *is* the order. Etyme’s award now raises the order and writes the contract as its first line."},{"etyme":"Requirement going down a chain · run: Chapter 1 — a one-person corporation registers on a gmail address › own consultant, listed on their own bench","sap":"a tiered supplier · subcontracting ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/first-real-transaction.test.ts the owner is already their a company of one has one role, and it is Owner","note":"The prime retypes the role for its sub under a band of its own; the sub never learns the end client unless the agreement requires disclosure."}],"png":"img/model/self-p2.png","sentences":0},{"code":"L1.2","name":"Contract to onboard","lanes":[{"name":"Who you sell to","sub":"prime · bench · client"},{"name":"The firm above you","sub":"its desks, doing the buying"},{"name":"You, as the firm","sub":"sells · insures · invoices"},{"name":"You, as the worker","sub":"files · is cleared · is paid"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Agreement, if new","sub":"both sign · optional","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":2,"title":"Countersign","sub":"the later date counts","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":3,"title":"Purchase order","sub":"the header · a ceiling","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":4,"title":"Sell line","sub":"this person, this rate","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":5,"title":"Buy line","sub":"pays the sub, or payroll","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":6,"title":"Our order to the sub","sub":"a ceiling of its own","lane":"You, as the firm"},{"n":7,"title":"Own W2 — no order","sub":"employment is the paper","lane":"You, as the worker"},{"n":8,"title":"Candidate green","sub":"I-9 · check · license","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":9,"title":"Papers","sub":"a link · no sign-in","lane":"You, as the worker"},{"n":10,"title":"Company green","sub":"insurance · terms","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":11,"title":"Insurance certificate","sub":"the start date is a floor","lane":"You, as the firm"},{"n":12,"title":"Activate","sub":"both lines move","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":13,"title":"Start date announced","sub":"not yet a moment","lane":"Who you sell to"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"Two gates, not one: the candidate is green and the company is green. The buy line forks — an order to a sub-vendor carries a ceiling; an employment to your own W2 carries no order at all, because you do not raise a purchase order to your own employee.","short":"Contract to onboard","page":3,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Agreement · MSA","sap":"an outline agreement · a sales contract","note":"Optional since 2026-09-18. Both signatures, and the date that matters is the later one. SAP has no countersignature of its own; that lives in a contracts tool. Never “master agreement” on a screen — “master contract” is the profitability roll-up, a different thing."},{"etyme":"Purchase order · sales order · work order","sap":"one order, mirrored: a PO on the buyer, a sales order on the seller","note":"One row, three names. The header: counterparty, ceiling, dates, terms, the four partner roles."},{"etyme":"Sell line — bills the customer","sap":"a sales-order item, one per worker","note":"A line on the order: this person, this rate, this site. What the firm bills from."},{"etyme":"Buy line to a sub-vendor — pays by invoice receipt","sap":"a service item on our order to the vendor","note":"Draws down our order to the sub. Rhythm and terms read from the document; the dates are the line’s own, because a line is a person."},{"etyme":"Buy line to own W2 — pays by payroll","sap":"a hiring action, not a vendor record","note":"No order to your own employee. SAP files the person under HR, never under purchasing."},{"etyme":"Supplier onboarding — four desks","sap":"supplier registration and qualification","note":"Etyme walks department lead, Procurement, HR and Finance in order, each verifying only its own items."},{"etyme":"Work authorization · I-9","sap":"a residence-status record on the person","note":"BLOCK. The form has an edition; an I-9 with nothing behind it is not held."},{"etyme":"Certificate of insurance","sap":"a supplier certificate with a validity window","note":"Etyme reads the start date as a floor — cover beginning next month does not cover somebody starting this week."},{"etyme":"Compliance · Agreement · Proof","sap":"—","note":"Etyme’s three purposes decide behavior. SAP scatters them across HR, procurement and document management."},{"etyme":"Activate","sap":"the hire · the release","note":"Both lines move together. Payment terms are not yet a gate."}],"png":"img/model/self-p3.png","sentences":11},{"code":"L1.3","name":"Work to approve","lanes":[{"name":"Who you sell to","sub":"prime · bench · client"},{"name":"The firm above you","sub":"its desks, doing the buying"},{"name":"You, as the firm","sub":"sells · insures · invoices"},{"name":"You, as the worker","sub":"files · is cleared · is paid"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"File the week","sub":"your own hours","lane":"You, as the worker"},{"n":2,"title":"Expense","sub":"receipt attached","lane":"You, as the worker"},{"n":3,"title":"Timesheet receipt","sub":"the goods receipt, here","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":4,"title":"Silence counts?","sub":"if the order says so","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":5,"title":"Pass-through","sub":"every rung, same hours","lane":"You, as the firm"},{"n":6,"title":"Checked vs contract","sub":"over hours · past end","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":7,"title":"Employer acceptance","sub":"what we will pay for","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":8,"title":"Milestone accepted","sub":"a receipt of another shape","lane":"Who you sell to"}],"refusals":[{"text":"nobody else may file it","lane":"You, as the worker","station":1}],"caption":"The goods receipt of a staffing firm is the signed week. SAP calls it a service entry sheet; the founder named it a timesheet receipt, and the screens use his word. Two signatures from two companies, one row of hours, never one per hop.","short":"Work to approve","page":5,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Timesheet","sap":"a time sheet","note":"The worker files their own week; the agency may enter on their behalf, nobody may sign for them."},{"etyme":"Timesheet receipt — client approval","sap":"the service entry sheet — the goods receipt for services","note":"Same object. “Our goods receipt equivalent is timesheet receipt or expense receipt.” The trade’s word wins on the screen."},{"etyme":"Employer acceptance","sap":"releasing the time sheet for pay","note":"SAP has one approval. Etyme has two signatures, because the client says the work happened and the employer says what it will pay for — different statements."},{"etyme":"Pass-through","sap":"tiered approval","note":"Each rung between the client and the worker sees the same hours it will bill and be billed for."},{"etyme":"Expense receipt","sap":"an expense report","note":"An approved, client-billable expense rides the next bill as a line of its own."},{"etyme":"Milestone receipt","sap":"a milestone on a billing plan","note":"Acceptance is the receipt; it bills as a milestone line."},{"etyme":"Auto-approval","sap":"an approval rule","note":"Read off the order: “silence counts” with a window. It fired for the first time on 2026-09-17, because no order row had ever existed to carry the flag."},{"etyme":"A week checked against its contract","sap":"—","note":"Over the role’s hours or past the last day says so in a sentence before anybody signs; “Approve anyway” takes a reason."}],"png":"img/model/self-p5.png","sentences":7},{"code":"L1.4","name":"Approve to invoice","lanes":[{"name":"Who you sell to","sub":"prime · bench · client"},{"name":"The firm above you","sub":"its desks, doing the buying"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Raise the bill","sub":"from the sell line","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":2,"title":"Four partners","sub":"sold-to · bill-to · ship-to · payer","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":3,"title":"Receives","sub":"receipt starts the clock","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":4,"title":"Pays what matched","sub":"never an unmatched bill","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":5,"title":"Cash application","sub":"a short payment is a question","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":6,"title":"Age & dun","sub":"from the due date, not period end","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":7,"title":"Dispute → credit note","sub":"reverses revenue","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":8,"title":"Exposure & limit","sub":"unpaid + unbilled + committed","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":9,"title":"Collections","sub":"stop-work · write-off","lane":"The firm above you"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"The firm bills its customer — SAP’s process is literally called billing, and the founder’s word matches it. The due date belongs to the document, counted from the day the client received it; nothing schedules one on the calendar to disagree with it.","short":"Approve to invoice","page":7,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Bill","sap":"billing — a billing document, a customer invoice","note":"Aligned by decision: “companies bill (also called invoice) a customer.”"},{"etyme":"Bill line — hours · expense · milestone","sap":"a billing item","note":"Three receipts, three kinds of line, one match."},{"etyme":"Sold-to · bill-to · ship-to · payer","sap":"the four partner roles on a sales document","note":"Identical concept. The first thing a large enterprise asks for."},{"etyme":"Tax","sap":"a tax code with a place of supply","note":"Regime, outcome and place of supply as queryable fields — a return cannot be filed from a blob."},{"etyme":"Cash application","sap":"an incoming payment · a lockbox","note":"A part payment is chased for the balance; a short payment is a question for a person, not arrears."},{"etyme":"Aging","sap":"customer open items","note":"Aged from the day each bill fell due, so sixty-day terms are not late on day forty-five."},{"etyme":"Dunning","sap":"a dunning run","note":"The ladder; who owns each step is a desk."},{"etyme":"Credit note","sap":"a credit memo","note":"A customer document we issue; it reverses revenue. Posted into the bill’s own period."},{"etyme":"Exposure · limit · run: Chapter 3 — the existing contract is recorded, both sides at once › be activated before it bills — a real step, not a bug","sap":"credit management ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/first-real-transaction.test.ts a recorded contract still has to Chapter 6 — the money is visible where a person would look for it › client owing the invoice","note":"Exposure is unpaid plus delivered-not-billed plus committed for the rest of every running assignment — which is why a client owing a little can be the riskiest name on the list. accounts receivable shows the"}],"png":"img/model/self-p7.png","sentences":0},{"code":"L1.5","name":"Approve to pay","lanes":[{"name":"You, as the firm","sub":"sells · insures · invoices"},{"name":"The firm above you","sub":"its desks, doing the buying"},{"name":"You, as the worker","sub":"files · is cleared · is paid"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Issues its invoice","sub":"their number, not ours","lane":"You, as the firm"},{"n":2,"title":"Invoice receipt","sub":"received, never raised","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":3,"title":"Three-way match","sub":"order ↔ receipt ↔ invoice","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":4,"title":"Exception → desk","sub":"a decision, with a reason","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":5,"title":"Payment run","sub":"approver is not the raiser","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":6,"title":"Remittance","sub":"what was paid, for what","lane":"You, as the firm"},{"n":7,"title":"Payroll","sub":"on accepted hours only","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":8,"title":"Paid","sub":"own pay · never the bill rate","lane":"You, as the worker"},{"n":9,"title":"Tax data → bureau","sub":"1099 · W-2 data","lane":"The firm above you"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"Money out in two directions, two words. A supplier’s invoice is received and matched — the invoice-receipt step. An employee is paid by payroll, which Fieldglass never touches because it stops at the supplier. The candidate sees what they are paid and never what a firm above them charges.","short":"Approve to pay","page":8,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Invoice receipt","sap":"invoice verification — the supplier’s invoice, received and matched","note":"The founder’s term is SAP’s term. The supplier issues the document; we receive it. Receiving it cannot need the permission to issue one of ours."},{"etyme":"Three-way match","sap":"order ↔ goods receipt ↔ invoice receipt","note":"Identical. Work order ↔ timesheet receipt ↔ supplier invoice. A client pays what came through the match."},{"etyme":"Match exception → the AP desk","sap":"a blocked invoice, released by a person","note":"A bill that did not match is a decision, with a reason recorded."},{"etyme":"Payment run","sap":"the automatic payment run","note":"An approver who is not the raiser."},{"etyme":"Remittance","sap":"a payment advice","note":""},{"etyme":"Payroll","sap":"payroll","note":"Fieldglass does not pay workers; it stops at the supplier. Payroll is the supplier’s own system."},{"etyme":"Pay model","sap":"wage types","note":"Salary, hourly, C2C, commission — applied per line."},{"etyme":"Bench reserve","sap":"—","note":"No SAP word. A firm holding back against bench time between projects."},{"etyme":"1099 · W-2 data","sap":"withholding and year-end reporting","note":"Data for the bureau, not the filing."},{"etyme":"Pay day shifts back; bill day shifts forward","sap":"a factory calendar · payment terms","note":"Per company, per category — before, after or neither — decided 2026-09-17 and wired into the dates the same day."}],"png":"img/model/self-p8.png","sentences":0},{"code":"L1.3 → L1.5","name":"An expense, from receipt to reimbursement","lanes":[{"name":"Who you sell to","sub":"prime · bench · client"},{"name":"The firm above you","sub":"its desks, doing the buying"},{"name":"You, as the firm","sub":"sells · insures · invoices"},{"name":"You, as the worker","sub":"files · is cleared · is paid"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Files an expense","sub":"amount · category · receipt","lane":"You, as the worker"},{"n":2,"title":"Billable to the client?","sub":"the order says; within the ceiling","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":3,"title":"Approves · or refuses","sub":"a reason travels with a refusal","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":4,"title":"Told the outcome","sub":"on their own channel","lane":"You, as the worker"},{"n":5,"title":"Pass-through","sub":"a sub’s person: same expense, every rung","lane":"You, as the firm"},{"n":6,"title":"Rides the next bill","sub":"an expense line of its own","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":7,"title":"Receives · matches","sub":"the approved expense is the receipt","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":8,"title":"Pays what matched","sub":"PAID with the bill","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":9,"title":"Reimburses the person","sub":"payroll, or the sub’s invoice","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":10,"title":"Its invoice carries it","sub":"received and matched, one rung down","lane":"You, as the firm"},{"n":11,"title":"Reimbursed","sub":"their own money back","lane":"You, as the worker"}],"refusals":[{"text":"nobody else may file it","lane":"You, as the worker","station":1}],"caption":"An expense is the second kind of receipt. The person files it with the paper behind it; the customer approves it or refuses it with a reason that travels with the record; an approved, client-billable expense rides the next bill as a line of its own, and the three-way match takes the approved expense as the receipt — an expense nobody approved never reaches a bill. It is paid with the bill, and reimbursed by whoever pays the person: payroll for an employee, the sub-vendor’s own invoice where a sub is below.","short":"Expenses","page":9,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Expense","sap":"an expense report · a trip","note":"Filed by the person against the placement, with the receipt attached. Nobody else may file it."},{"etyme":"Expense receipt — the customer’s approval","sap":"an approved expense report","note":"The founder’s word: “our goods receipt equivalent is timesheet receipt or expense receipt.” The approval is the receipt."},{"etyme":"Refusal, with a reason","sap":"a rejected expense item","note":"The reason travels with the record and reaches the person on their own channel."},{"etyme":"Expense line on the bill","sap":"a billing item for expenses · re-billing","note":"Rides the next bill as a line of its own, beside the hours lines, and is PAID with it."},{"etyme":"Match: line ↔ approved expense","sap":"the three-way match, receipt-side","note":"Order ↔ approved expense ↔ bill line. An expense nobody approved never bills."},{"etyme":"Reimbursement","sap":"payroll or the vendor’s invoice","note":"Whoever pays the person reimburses them: payroll for an employee; a sub-vendor’s own invoice carries it one rung down."},{"etyme":"Client-billable or not","sap":"a cost assignment on the item","note":"Read off the order the placement is a line on; a non-billable expense stops at the employer and never reaches the customer."}],"png":"img/model/self-p9.png","sentences":0},{"code":"L1.6","name":"Record to report","lanes":[{"name":"The firm above you","sub":"its desks, doing the buying"},{"name":"ERP","sub":"the books"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Receipt posted","sub":"cost · payable","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":2,"title":"Payroll posted","sub":"pay · burden","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":3,"title":"Journal","sub":"one balanced entry each","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":4,"title":"Master contract","sub":"optional tag · the roll-up","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":5,"title":"Profitability","sub":"margin, by the deal","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":6,"title":"Earned vs cash","sub":"days to get paid, real months","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":7,"title":"Account map","sub":"our words → their accounts","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":8,"title":"Outbound posting","sub":"to the books they keep","lane":"ERP"},{"n":9,"title":"Reconciliation","sub":"read back, differences owned","lane":"ERP"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"Etyme posts into the books; it does not replace them. The mapping is stated once at the boundary: QuickBooks and Xero say Invoice for the customer document and Bill for the received one — their Invoice is our bill, their Bill is our invoice receipt.","short":"Record to report","page":10,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Journal","sap":"the general ledger · a universal journal","note":"Every posting turns into a balanced entry; the receivable move on every bill and the cash move on every applied receipt."},{"etyme":"The pair — a sell line and the buy line that funds it","sap":"a sales item and a purchase item settled to one cost object","note":"A placement’s own margin. Always written by the award, because a buy line pays for some sell line."},{"etyme":"Master contract — the profitability roll-up","sap":"an internal order · a work-breakdown element","note":"The Etyme-2017 word, kept: the container that once held both sides on one row is now an optional tag. A company tags sell and buy lines to one when it wants to see the deal’s margin. Not a commercial document; nobody signs one — same in SAP, where the sales order and the purchase order both settle to it."},{"etyme":"Profitability by pair, person, customer, master","sap":"margin analysis","note":"Read from real revenue and cost; gated on the right to read P&L, which the account manager deliberately does not hold."},{"etyme":"Earned against cash","sap":"revenue recognition","note":"Days to get paid counted back through real months rather than divided by an average, so growth does not move it."},{"etyme":"Currency","sap":"currency types and exchange rates","note":"Money in minor units, always."},{"etyme":"ERP account map","sap":"the chart of accounts · an integration","note":"Businesses pay for QuickBooks, SAP and NetSuite directly; Etyme posts to them."},{"etyme":"Reconciliation · run: Chapter 4 — a week is worked and approved by both parties › the approval posted real money to a real project order","sap":"clearing · a bank statement ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/first-real-transaction.test.ts Chapter 6 — the money is visible where a person would look for it › margin, not a fabricated one","note":"Reads the books back; a difference is a row somebody owns. profitability reports the real"}],"png":"img/model/self-p10.png","sentences":0},{"code":"L1.7","name":"Govern and protect","lanes":[{"name":"Who you sell to","sub":"prime · bench · client"},{"name":"The firm above you","sub":"its desks, doing the buying"},{"name":"Etyme, unprompted","sub":"what it does on its own"},{"name":"You, as the firm","sub":"sells · insures · invoices"},{"name":"You, as the worker","sub":"files · is cleared · is paid"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Tenure ledger","sub":"the person, at the client","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":2,"title":"Days on site","sub":"counted once per day","lane":"Who you sell to"},{"n":3,"title":"Classification","sub":"W2 · 1099 · C2C","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":4,"title":"Approval chains","sub":"by rule and by name","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":5,"title":"Segregation","sub":"nobody decides two desks","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":6,"title":"Supplier standing","sub":"probation · approved · preferred","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":7,"title":"Insured · authorized","sub":"the client always sees this","lane":"You, as the firm"},{"n":8,"title":"Concentration","sub":"one client, one person","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":9,"title":"Access log","sub":"every read · refusals too","lane":"Etyme, unprompted"},{"n":10,"title":"Automation log","sub":"why · and can it be undone","lane":"Etyme, unprompted"},{"n":11,"title":"Do-not-return list","sub":"the company’s own","lane":"The firm above you"},{"n":12,"title":"Told what is held","sub":"own pay only","lane":"You, as the worker"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"The moat, not the wedge: tenure accrues to the person at the client across every supplier, counted once per day on site. SAP records what changed; Etyme also records why, and whether it can be undone — and every read of another person’s data leaves a row, including the refusals.","short":"Govern and protect","page":11,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Tenure — the person at the client, across suppliers","sap":"a tenure policy · contract elements on the person","note":"Fieldglass tracks tenure per worker at the buyer within its own walls. Etyme’s claim is across suppliers who are not all on one system — which is every buyer who cannot afford one."},{"etyme":"Worker classification","sap":"employee group and subgroup","note":"BLOCK where legally grounded."},{"etyme":"Approval chain","sap":"a release strategy · a workflow","note":"Most requisitions must clear without a human. A desk nobody named falls back; it never refuses."},{"etyme":"Segregation of duties","sap":"an access-control ruleset","note":"“You recommended this firm, so the desks decide it without you.” A sentence, never a disabled button."},{"etyme":"Supplier standing","sap":"supplier risk","note":"Probation · approved · preferred, read by the tier rule."},{"etyme":"Concentration","sap":"margin analysis by customer","note":"Revenue share riding on one client, one supplier, one person, with a named risk owner."},{"etyme":"Access log — every read of a person","sap":"an audit log · read-access logging","note":"The nearest thing logs reads of sensitive fields. Etyme logs the refusals too."},{"etyme":"Company walls","sap":"authorization objects · company codes","note":"A caller with no company is refused, never handed every company’s list."},{"etyme":"Automation log — what the system did on its own","sap":"change documents","note":"SAP records what changed. Etyme records the plain-English reason and an honest reversible flag, and every action name is declared on a ladder."},{"etyme":"Do-not-return list","sap":"a vendor block · a rehire flag","note":"Read by every desk that puts people forward; written by the desk that owns who goes forward. Never read across companies."},{"etyme":"Whose rate is on the row","sap":"rate visibility","note":"The person named on a sell line is the subject of it, not a party to it."},{"etyme":"What we tell people about their data","sap":"information lifecycle · data privacy","note":"A page of their own, off until they turn it on."},{"etyme":"Insured · authorized — the client always sees this · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/standing-and-seats.test.ts standing, units and cold seats › Northbend Athletic rates Pinnacle on probation and Brightmoor preferred, and the suppliers page says so","sap":"a word not on the list is refused in a sentence Northbend Athletic adds a Data practice under Technology; adding it twice hands back the first","note":"a kind the schema does not name is refused a seat nobody has advertised in eight weeks goes cold overnight; one seen last week stays live"}],"png":"img/model/self-p11.png","sentences":7}]},{"meta":{"key":"candidate","number":"8A","name":"Candidate — on a bench","label":"Candidate on a bench","tagline":"Listed by a firm you chose. It pays you; a prime may sell you on; the site signs your week.","position":"You granted a bench listing to one firm — the consent that lets it put you forward — and can take it back. That firm pays you, by payroll or corp-to-corp. A prime above it may sell you on to a client that thinks the prime employs you. You file your own week and nobody else may; you are told your pay and never what anybody above you charges.","desks":["You"],"doors":["Helena","Marsh /demo · helena-marsh","Chidi","Okafor /demo · chidi-okafor"],"how":"","summary":"Helena Marsh is on a bench vendor’s books and sold on to a sportswear company by the prime above it, two hundred days on site against an eighteen-month cap. Chidi Okafor is two rungs down a chain on an H1B, with a site-access attestation only he can sign. From here the firm that lists you and every rung above it collapse to two lanes, because that is all you can see — and by design: the sub- vendor’s name is the prime’s to keep, and the rate above you is nobody’s to show you. Shaded lane — a party outside the firm. Anything crossing into it is a document a counterparty reads. Blue-edged lane — one of this party’s own desks. Its boxes are solid; everyone else’s are faded but still there, because the stream does not change — only who is looking. Labelled arrow — the artifact that moves: requisition, submission, order, timesheet receipt, bill, invoice. Dashed box — a station the operating m"},"streams":[{"code":"L1.1","name":"Source to contract","lanes":[{"name":"The prime that sold you on","sub":"and the client behind it"},{"name":"The firm that lists you","sub":"your bench vendor; it pays you"},{"name":"You","sub":"listed; the listing is yours"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Raise requisition","sub":"the role, the months, the rate","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":2,"title":"Three desks clear it","sub":"HR · Procurement · the lead","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":3,"title":"Release to suppliers","sub":"the ones Procurement cleared","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":4,"title":"Accept · pass down","sub":"a band of its own","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":5,"title":"Source & match","sub":"a score says why","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":6,"title":"Consent to represent","sub":"the listing — yours to give","lane":"You"},{"n":7,"title":"Submit","sub":"a rate, at this rung","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":8,"title":"Shortlist · negotiate","sub":"right-to-work first","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":9,"title":"Interview","sub":"rounds in turn","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":10,"title":"Award","sub":"the order and its first line","lane":"The prime that sold you on"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"One requisition becomes one award. It clears three desks first — HR reads the role, Procurement audits the suppliers, the lead who owns the cost center signs the money — and nobody signs their own; within plan every desk clears by rule and it publishes itself. Every arrow that crosses into a shaded lane is a document a counterparty reads — and the rate band travels on the invitation, never on the requisition, so no supplier reads another’s.","short":"Source to contract","page":2,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Requisition","sap":"a purchase requisition · a job posting","note":"Same object. Etyme clears it through three desks — HR reads the role, Procurement audits the suppliers, the cost-center lead signs the money; SAP puts a release strategy on it."},{"etyme":"Rate band","sap":"a rate guideline · a price on the vendor record","note":"Both keep the price per supplier where no other supplier can read it. Etyme puts it on the invitation."},{"etyme":"Supplier release","sap":"a request for quotation to the source list","note":"“These vendors may quote.” The program office decides, never the hiring manager."},{"etyme":"Bench listing — consent to be marketed","sap":"—","note":"No SAP word. Fieldglass has a worker profile; nobody in SAP consents to be sold. The invariant with no counterpart."},{"etyme":"Submission","sap":"a quotation · a job-seeker submittal","note":"A quotation at a rate, one per rung of the chain — two rows, one chain."},{"etyme":"Interview","sap":"an interview","note":"Only whoever is hiring may set up or decide a round."},{"etyme":"Award","sap":"creating the purchase order · creating the work order","note":"In SAP the award *is* the order. Etyme’s award now raises the order and writes the contract as its first line."},{"etyme":"Requirement going down a chain · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/bench-invitation.test.ts adding somebody to a bench is a question, not a fact › creates the listing as invited rather than granted records the invitation as a message, so somebody can see it was sent · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/contractor-invite.test.ts","sap":"a tiered supplier · subcontracting refuses to submit them while the invitation is unanswered and the consultant answers without an account › by opening it","note":"The prime retypes the role for its sub under a band of its own; the sub never learns the end client unless the agreement requires disclosure. accepts, and the grant is stamped when they agreed opens the link and is asked, with nothing changed cannot be answered twice and now the submission goes through"}],"png":"img/model/candidate-p2.png","sentences":58},{"code":"L1.2","name":"Contract to onboard","lanes":[{"name":"The prime that sold you on","sub":"and the client behind it"},{"name":"The firm that lists you","sub":"your bench vendor; it pays you"},{"name":"You","sub":"listed; the listing is yours"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Agreement, if new","sub":"both sign · optional","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":2,"title":"Countersign","sub":"the later date counts","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":3,"title":"Purchase order","sub":"the header · a ceiling","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":4,"title":"Sell line","sub":"this person, this rate","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":5,"title":"Buy line","sub":"pays the sub, or payroll","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":6,"title":"Own W2 — no order","sub":"employment is the paper","lane":"You"},{"n":7,"title":"Candidate green","sub":"I-9 · check · license","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":8,"title":"Papers","sub":"a link · no sign-in","lane":"You"},{"n":9,"title":"Company green","sub":"insurance · terms","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":10,"title":"Activate","sub":"both lines move","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":11,"title":"Start date announced","sub":"not yet a moment","lane":"The prime that sold you on"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"Two gates, not one: the candidate is green and the company is green. The buy line forks — an order to a sub-vendor carries a ceiling; an employment to your own W2 carries no order at all, because you do not raise a purchase order to your own employee.","short":"Contract to onboard","page":4,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Agreement · MSA","sap":"an outline agreement · a sales contract","note":"Optional since 2026-09-18. Both signatures, and the date that matters is the later one. SAP has no countersignature of its own; that lives in a contracts tool. Never “master agreement” on a screen — “master contract” is the profitability roll-up, a different thing."},{"etyme":"Purchase order · sales order · work order","sap":"one order, mirrored: a PO on the buyer, a sales order on the seller","note":"One row, three names. The header: counterparty, ceiling, dates, terms, the four partner roles."},{"etyme":"Sell line — bills the customer","sap":"a sales-order item, one per worker","note":"A line on the order: this person, this rate, this site. What the firm bills from."},{"etyme":"Buy line to a sub-vendor — pays by invoice receipt","sap":"a service item on our order to the vendor","note":"Draws down our order to the sub. Rhythm and terms read from the document; the dates are the line’s own, because a line is a person."},{"etyme":"Buy line to own W2 — pays by payroll","sap":"a hiring action, not a vendor record","note":"No order to your own employee. SAP files the person under HR, never under purchasing."},{"etyme":"Supplier onboarding — four desks","sap":"supplier registration and qualification","note":"Etyme walks department lead, Procurement, HR and Finance in order, each verifying only its own items."},{"etyme":"Work authorization · I-9","sap":"a residence-status record on the person","note":"BLOCK. The form has an edition; an I-9 with nothing behind it is not held."},{"etyme":"Certificate of insurance","sap":"a supplier certificate with a validity window","note":"Etyme reads the start date as a floor — cover beginning next month does not cover somebody starting this week."},{"etyme":"Compliance · Agreement · Proof","sap":"—","note":"Etyme’s three purposes decide behavior. SAP scatters them across HR, procurement and document management."},{"etyme":"Activate","sap":"the hire · the release","note":"Both lines move together. Payment terms are not yet a gate."},{"etyme":"Own W2 — no order — employment is the paper","sap":"","note":""}],"png":"img/model/candidate-p4.png","sentences":74},{"code":"L1.3","name":"Work to approve","lanes":[{"name":"The prime that sold you on","sub":"and the client behind it"},{"name":"The firm that lists you","sub":"your bench vendor; it pays you"},{"name":"You","sub":"listed; the listing is yours"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"File the week","sub":"your own hours","lane":"You"},{"n":2,"title":"Expense","sub":"receipt attached","lane":"You"},{"n":3,"title":"Timesheet receipt","sub":"the goods receipt, here","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":4,"title":"Silence counts?","sub":"if the order says so","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":5,"title":"Checked vs contract","sub":"over hours · past end","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":6,"title":"Employer acceptance","sub":"what we will pay for","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":7,"title":"Milestone accepted","sub":"a receipt of another shape","lane":"The prime that sold you on"}],"refusals":[{"text":"nobody else may file it","lane":"You","station":1}],"caption":"The goods receipt of a staffing firm is the signed week. SAP calls it a service entry sheet; the founder named it a timesheet receipt, and the screens use his word. Two signatures from two companies, one row of hours, never one per hop.","short":"Work to approve","page":7,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Timesheet","sap":"a time sheet","note":"The worker files their own week; the agency may enter on their behalf, nobody may sign for them."},{"etyme":"Timesheet receipt — client approval","sap":"the service entry sheet — the goods receipt for services","note":"Same object. “Our goods receipt equivalent is timesheet receipt or expense receipt.” The trade’s word wins on the screen."},{"etyme":"Employer acceptance","sap":"releasing the time sheet for pay","note":"SAP has one approval. Etyme has two signatures, because the client says the work happened and the employer says what it will pay for — different statements."},{"etyme":"Pass-through","sap":"tiered approval","note":"Each rung between the client and the worker sees the same hours it will bill and be billed for."},{"etyme":"Expense receipt","sap":"an expense report","note":"An approved, client-billable expense rides the next bill as a line of its own."},{"etyme":"Milestone receipt","sap":"a milestone on a billing plan","note":"Acceptance is the receipt; it bills as a milestone line."},{"etyme":"Auto-approval","sap":"an approval rule","note":"Read off the order: “silence counts” with a window. It fired for the first time on 2026-09-17, because no order row had ever existed to carry the flag."},{"etyme":"A week checked against its contract · run:","sap":"— ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/first-real-transaction.test.ts","note":"Over the role’s hours or past the last day says so in a sentence before anybody signs; “Approve anyway” takes a reason."}],"png":"img/model/candidate-p7.png","sentences":16},{"code":"L1.4","name":"Approve to invoice","lanes":[{"name":"The prime that sold you on","sub":"and the client behind it"},{"name":"The firm that lists you","sub":"your bench vendor; it pays you"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Raise the bill","sub":"from the sell line","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":2,"title":"Four partners","sub":"sold-to · bill-to · ship-to · payer","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":3,"title":"Receives","sub":"receipt starts the clock","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":4,"title":"Pays what matched","sub":"never an unmatched bill","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":5,"title":"Cash application","sub":"a short payment is a question","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":6,"title":"Age & dun","sub":"from the due date, not period end","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":7,"title":"Dispute → credit note","sub":"reverses revenue","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":8,"title":"Exposure & limit","sub":"unpaid + unbilled + committed","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":9,"title":"Collections","sub":"stop-work · write-off","lane":"The firm that lists you"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"The firm bills its customer — SAP’s process is literally called billing, and the founder’s word matches it. The due date belongs to the document, counted from the day the client received it; nothing schedules one on the calendar to disagree with it.","short":"Approve to invoice","page":9,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Bill","sap":"billing — a billing document, a customer invoice","note":"Aligned by decision: “companies bill (also called invoice) a customer.”"},{"etyme":"Bill line — hours · expense · milestone","sap":"a billing item","note":"Three receipts, three kinds of line, one match."},{"etyme":"Sold-to · bill-to · ship-to · payer","sap":"the four partner roles on a sales document","note":"Identical concept. The first thing a large enterprise asks for."},{"etyme":"Tax","sap":"a tax code with a place of supply","note":"Regime, outcome and place of supply as queryable fields — a return cannot be filed from a blob."},{"etyme":"Cash application","sap":"an incoming payment · a lockbox","note":"A part payment is chased for the balance; a short payment is a question for a person, not arrears."},{"etyme":"Aging","sap":"customer open items","note":"Aged from the day each bill fell due, so sixty-day terms are not late on day forty-five."},{"etyme":"Dunning","sap":"a dunning run","note":"The ladder; who owns each step is a desk."},{"etyme":"Credit note","sap":"a credit memo","note":"A customer document we issue; it reverses revenue. Posted into the bill’s own period."},{"etyme":"Exposure · limit · run: Chapter 3 — the existing contract is recorded, both sides at once › be activated before it bills — a real step, not a bug · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/two-hop-chain.test.ts","sap":"credit management ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/first-real-transaction.test.ts a recorded contract still has to Chapter 6 — the money is visible where a person would look for it › client owing the invoice","note":"Exposure is unpaid plus delivered-not-billed plus committed for the rest of every running assignment — which is why a client owing a little can be the riskiest name on the list. accounts receivable shows the"}],"png":"img/model/candidate-p9.png","sentences":4},{"code":"L1.5","name":"Approve to pay","lanes":[{"name":"The firm that lists you","sub":"your bench vendor; it pays you"},{"name":"You","sub":"listed; the listing is yours"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Invoice receipt","sub":"received, never raised","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":2,"title":"Three-way match","sub":"order ↔ receipt ↔ invoice","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":3,"title":"Exception → desk","sub":"a decision, with a reason","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":4,"title":"Payment run","sub":"approver is not the raiser","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":5,"title":"Payroll","sub":"on accepted hours only","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":6,"title":"Paid","sub":"own pay · never the bill rate","lane":"You"},{"n":7,"title":"Tax data → bureau","sub":"1099 · W-2 data","lane":"The firm that lists you"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"Money out in two directions, two words. A supplier’s invoice is received and matched — the invoice-receipt step. An employee is paid by payroll, which Fieldglass never touches because it stops at the supplier. The candidate sees what they are paid and never what a firm above them charges.","short":"Approve to pay","page":11,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Invoice receipt","sap":"invoice verification — the supplier’s invoice, received and matched","note":"The founder’s term is SAP’s term. The supplier issues the document; we receive it. Receiving it cannot need the permission to issue one of ours."},{"etyme":"Three-way match","sap":"order ↔ goods receipt ↔ invoice receipt","note":"Identical. Work order ↔ timesheet receipt ↔ supplier invoice. A client pays what came through the match."},{"etyme":"Match exception → the AP desk","sap":"a blocked invoice, released by a person","note":"A bill that did not match is a decision, with a reason recorded."},{"etyme":"Payment run","sap":"the automatic payment run","note":"An approver who is not the raiser."},{"etyme":"Remittance","sap":"a payment advice","note":""},{"etyme":"Payroll","sap":"payroll","note":"Fieldglass does not pay workers; it stops at the supplier. Payroll is the supplier’s own system."},{"etyme":"Pay model","sap":"wage types","note":"Salary, hourly, C2C, commission — applied per line."},{"etyme":"Bench reserve","sap":"—","note":"No SAP word. A firm holding back against bench time between projects."},{"etyme":"1099 · W-2 data","sap":"withholding and year-end reporting","note":"Data for the bureau, not the filing."},{"etyme":"Pay day shifts back; bill day shifts forward · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/full-spine.test.ts Step 13 — the contracts are activated, and the PO is attached › activates both buy contracts so payroll has something to pay against · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/gsi-payroll.test.ts","sap":"a factory calendar · payment terms Step 17 — CloudEPA pays Priya › owes her 40 hours at $85 — $3,400","note":"Per company, per category — before, after or neither — decided 2026-09-17 and wired into the dates the same day."}],"png":"img/model/candidate-p11.png","sentences":11},{"code":"L1.3 → L1.5","name":"An expense, from receipt to reimbursement","lanes":[{"name":"The prime that sold you on","sub":"and the client behind it"},{"name":"The firm that lists you","sub":"your bench vendor; it pays you"},{"name":"You","sub":"listed; the listing is yours"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Files an expense","sub":"amount · category · receipt","lane":"You"},{"n":2,"title":"Billable to the client?","sub":"the order says; within the ceiling","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":3,"title":"Approves · or refuses","sub":"a reason travels with a refusal","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":4,"title":"Told the outcome","sub":"on their own channel","lane":"You"},{"n":5,"title":"Rides the next bill","sub":"an expense line of its own","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":6,"title":"Receives · matches","sub":"the approved expense is the receipt","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":7,"title":"Pays what matched","sub":"PAID with the bill","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":8,"title":"Reimburses the person","sub":"payroll, or the sub’s invoice","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":9,"title":"Reimbursed","sub":"their own money back","lane":"You"}],"refusals":[{"text":"nobody else may file it","lane":"You","station":1}],"caption":"An expense is the second kind of receipt. The person files it with the paper behind it; the customer approves it or refuses it with a reason that travels with the record; an approved, client-billable expense rides the next bill as a line of its own, and the three-way match takes the approved expense as the receipt — an expense nobody approved never reaches a bill. It is paid with the bill, and reimbursed by whoever pays the person: payroll for an employee, the sub-vendor’s own invoice where a sub is below.","short":"Expenses","page":13,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Expense","sap":"an expense report · a trip","note":"Filed by the person against the placement, with the receipt attached. Nobody else may file it."},{"etyme":"Expense receipt — the customer’s approval","sap":"an approved expense report","note":"The founder’s word: “our goods receipt equivalent is timesheet receipt or expense receipt.” The approval is the receipt."},{"etyme":"Refusal, with a reason","sap":"a rejected expense item","note":"The reason travels with the record and reaches the person on their own channel."},{"etyme":"Expense line on the bill","sap":"a billing item for expenses · re-billing","note":"Rides the next bill as a line of its own, beside the hours lines, and is PAID with it."},{"etyme":"Match: line ↔ approved expense","sap":"the three-way match, receipt-side","note":"Order ↔ approved expense ↔ bill line. An expense nobody approved never bills."},{"etyme":"Reimbursement","sap":"payroll or the vendor’s invoice","note":"Whoever pays the person reimburses them: payroll for an employee; a sub-vendor’s own invoice carries it one rung down."},{"etyme":"Client-billable or not · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/status-ledger.test.ts the ledger: one placement, every table, every station › a flight Tariq paid for: expense DRAFT, SUBMITTED, APPROVED","sap":"a cost assignment on the item the invoice: ISSUED on raising with the expense on it as INVOICED, SUBMITTED on sending, and the invoice-to-raise cycle is done","note":"Read off the order the placement is a line on; a non-billable expense stops at the employer and never reaches the customer. the payment: invoice PAID with its expense, and a payment row saying who paid whom"}],"png":"img/model/candidate-p13.png","sentences":0},{"code":"L1.6","name":"Record to report","lanes":[{"name":"The firm that lists you","sub":"your bench vendor; it pays you"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Receipt posted","sub":"cost · payable","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":2,"title":"Payroll posted","sub":"pay · burden","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":3,"title":"Journal","sub":"one balanced entry each","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":4,"title":"Master contract","sub":"optional tag · the roll-up","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":5,"title":"Profitability","sub":"margin, by the deal","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":6,"title":"Earned vs cash","sub":"days to get paid, real months","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":7,"title":"Account map","sub":"our words → their accounts","lane":"The firm that lists you"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"Etyme posts into the books; it does not replace them. The mapping is stated once at the boundary: QuickBooks and Xero say Invoice for the customer document and Bill for the received one — their Invoice is our bill, their Bill is our invoice receipt.","short":"Record to report","page":14,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Journal","sap":"the general ledger · a universal journal","note":"Every posting turns into a balanced entry; the receivable move on every bill and the cash move on every applied receipt."},{"etyme":"The pair — a sell line and the buy line that funds it","sap":"a sales item and a purchase item settled to one cost object","note":"A placement’s own margin. Always written by the award, because a buy line pays for some sell line."},{"etyme":"Master contract — the profitability roll-up","sap":"an internal order · a work-breakdown element","note":"The Etyme-2017 word, kept: the container that once held both sides on one row is now an optional tag. A company tags sell and buy lines to one when it wants to see the deal’s margin. Not a commercial document; nobody signs one — same in SAP, where the sales order and the purchase order both settle to it."},{"etyme":"Profitability by pair, person, customer, master","sap":"margin analysis","note":"Read from real revenue and cost; gated on the right to read P&L, which the account manager deliberately does not hold."},{"etyme":"Earned against cash","sap":"revenue recognition","note":"Days to get paid counted back through real months rather than divided by an average, so growth does not move it."},{"etyme":"Currency","sap":"currency types and exchange rates","note":"Money in minor units, always."},{"etyme":"ERP account map","sap":"the chart of accounts · an integration","note":"Businesses pay for QuickBooks, SAP and NetSuite directly; Etyme posts to them."},{"etyme":"Reconciliation · run: Chapter 4 — a week is worked and approved by both parties › the approval posted real money to a real project order · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/full-spine.test.ts Step 19 — the same week reaches Auralis, at Auralis’s rate › has moved $5,400 from Auralis to $3,400 in Priya’s hands, with $1,000 kept at each hop · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/status-ledger.test.ts","sap":"clearing · a bank statement ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/first-real-transaction.test.ts Chapter 6 — the money is visible where a person would look for it › margin, not a fabricated one","note":"Reads the books back; a difference is a row somebody owns. profitability reports the real"}],"png":"img/model/candidate-p14.png","sentences":14},{"code":"L1.7","name":"Govern and protect","lanes":[{"name":"The prime that sold you on","sub":"and the client behind it"},{"name":"The firm that lists you","sub":"your bench vendor; it pays you"},{"name":"Etyme","sub":"what it tells you"},{"name":"You","sub":"listed; the listing is yours"}],"stations":[{"n":1,"title":"Tenure ledger","sub":"the person, at the client","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":2,"title":"Days on site","sub":"counted once per day","lane":"The prime that sold you on"},{"n":3,"title":"Classification","sub":"W2 · 1099 · C2C","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":4,"title":"Approval chains","sub":"by rule and by name","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":5,"title":"Segregation","sub":"nobody decides two desks","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":6,"title":"Supplier standing","sub":"probation · approved · preferred","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":7,"title":"Concentration","sub":"one client, one person","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":8,"title":"Access log","sub":"every read · refusals too","lane":"Etyme"},{"n":9,"title":"Automation log","sub":"why · and can it be undone","lane":"Etyme"},{"n":10,"title":"Do-not-return list","sub":"the company’s own","lane":"The firm that lists you"},{"n":11,"title":"Told what is held","sub":"own pay only","lane":"You"}],"refusals":[],"caption":"The moat, not the wedge: tenure accrues to the person at the client across every supplier, counted once per day on site. SAP records what changed; Etyme also records why, and whether it can be undone — and every read of another person’s data leaves a row, including the refusals.","short":"Govern and protect","page":16,"glossary":[{"etyme":"Tenure — the person at the client, across suppliers","sap":"a tenure policy · contract elements on the person","note":"Fieldglass tracks tenure per worker at the buyer within its own walls. Etyme’s claim is across suppliers who are not all on one system — which is every buyer who cannot afford one."},{"etyme":"Worker classification","sap":"employee group and subgroup","note":"BLOCK where legally grounded."},{"etyme":"Approval chain","sap":"a release strategy · a workflow","note":"Most requisitions must clear without a human. A desk nobody named falls back; it never refuses."},{"etyme":"Segregation of duties","sap":"an access-control ruleset","note":"“You recommended this firm, so the desks decide it without you.” A sentence, never a disabled button."},{"etyme":"Supplier standing","sap":"supplier risk","note":"Probation · approved · preferred, read by the tier rule."},{"etyme":"Concentration","sap":"margin analysis by customer","note":"Revenue share riding on one client, one supplier, one person, with a named risk owner."},{"etyme":"Access log — every read of a person","sap":"an audit log · read-access logging","note":"The nearest thing logs reads of sensitive fields. Etyme logs the refusals too."},{"etyme":"Company walls","sap":"authorization objects · company codes","note":"A caller with no company is refused, never handed every company’s list."},{"etyme":"Automation log — what the system did on its own","sap":"change documents","note":"SAP records what changed. Etyme records the plain-English reason and an honest reversible flag, and every action name is declared on a ladder."},{"etyme":"Do-not-return list","sap":"a vendor block · a rehire flag","note":"Read by every desk that puts people forward; written by the desk that owns who goes forward. Never read across companies."},{"etyme":"Whose rate is on the row","sap":"rate visibility","note":"The person named on a sell line is the subject of it, not a party to it."},{"etyme":"What we tell people about their data · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/full-spine.test.ts Step 21 — one placement, opened, top to bottom › writes an access log row for the refusal as well as the read · run: ETYME_TEST_DB=etyme_test_walk npx vitest run -c vitest.integration.config.ts __integration__/whose-rate.test.ts a client sees the rate it pays, never the rate its supplier pays underneath › the first place, or this test proves nothing shows the hiring manager $145 an hour and never $118 never puts a supplier’s cost anywhere on the client’s whole list names the firm Northbend Athletic pays on the row, not the firm its prime pays the same person bought through a chain is one row and one rate on the client’s list › one week per week, not one per rung carries one rate per row, and it is the same rate on every one of them","sap":"information lifecycle · data privacy has a chain to read in what a client has approved is valued at the rate that client is billed › $145 an hour understated the client by the prime’s margin when it read the leg underneath a consultant sees what they are paid and never what they are billed at › session can reach and finds their own pay on it shows them only their own weeks, never the agency’s book gives Helena values their week at their own rate, so the markup never appears as a total either nobody is shown a button the server will refuse them › own week","note":"A page of their own, off until they turn it on. values her approved weeks at offers the hiring manager the signature, because the buyer says the work happened tenure counts days actually served, never the length of the contract › reads the same months on the contractors page as on the tenure page opens the page their does not say Helena is past a cap she is halfway to says the day somebody starts, for somebody who has not started yet what a client has spent is counted at the desk that signed for it › charges a week filed on a supplier\\u2019s own leg to the cost center that owns the role offers the consultant no signature on their a person bought through two legs of one chain has served one set of days, not two › counts Helena’s chain once, the way lib/chain-top counts it on the dashboard"}],"png":"img/model/candidate-p16.png","sentences":26}]}],"invariants":134};
